window.GUIDE_DATA = [{"id":"getting-started","label":"Getting Started","items":[{"id":"1","number":"1","title":"How to Use This Guide","fullTitle":"1. How to Use This Guide","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">FASTEST PATH</span> If you know the task, jump directly to its procedure. Read the Policy / Rule box first. Continue into the steps only if you need execution help.</div><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Element</strong></th>\n<th><strong>What it tells you</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Policy / Rule</td>\n<td>The non-negotiable requirement or operating standard.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Use when</td>\n<td>The trigger for the procedure.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Before you start</td>\n<td>What to verify before changing the booking or promising an outcome.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Steps</td>\n<td>The operating sequence from intake through completion.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>If / Then</td>\n<td>Decision points, exceptions, or alternate paths.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Document</td>\n<td>What must be left in Plex/Zendesk or communicated.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Escalate when</td>\n<td>The point at which CS should not proceed independently.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Complete when</td>\n<td>The condition that means the work is actually finished.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"FASTEST PATH If you know the task, jump directly to its procedure. Read the Policy / Rule box first. Continue into the steps only if you need execution help. Element What it tells you Policy / Rule The non-negotiable requirement or operating standard. Use when The trigger for the procedure. Before you start What to verify before changing the booking or promising an outcome. Steps The operating sequence from intake through completion. If / Then Decision points, exceptions, or alternate paths. Document What must be left in Plex/Zendesk or communicated. Escalate when The point at which CS should not proceed independently. Complete when The condition that means the work is actually finished.","blocks":[{"id":"1-2","heading":"1.2 Quick Task Finder","html":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>I need to…</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Go to</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Help a traveler currently in destination</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#8\">8. Hotel </a>/ <a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#9\">9. Transfers </a>/ <a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#10\">10. Air</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Move a traveler to another hotel</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#8\">8. Hotel In-Travel Assistance</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process a refund</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#12\">12. Cancellations, Penalties &amp; Refunds</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Partially refund a hotel night/service</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#13\">13. Financial Adjustments</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protect or recall commission</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#14\">14. Commission</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Offer goodwill or a future travel credit</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#16\">16. Goodwill &amp; Service Recovery</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Answer a TSP question</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#17\">17. Trip Protection</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hotel says the VCC is missing/declining</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#15\">15. VCC / Hotel Payment Support</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hotel charged the traveler directly</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#15\">15. VCC / Hotel Payment Support</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Build or extend an in-travel component</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#18\">18. CAD &amp; Manual Components</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Work a Group issue</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#19\">19. Groups</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Escalate a Preferred supplier</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#20\">20. Supplier / Product Escalation</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Move a case to Post-Travel</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#21\">21. Post-Travel</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get a supervisor involved</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#22\">22. Leadership Escalations</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Know what to put in notes</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#23\">23. Documentation</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Route a Finance question</td>\n<td><a class=\"cross-ref\" href=\"#24\">24. Finance Operations Routing</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","text":"I need to… Go to Help a traveler currently in destination 8. Hotel / 9. Transfers / 10. Air Move a traveler to another hotel 8. Hotel In-Travel Assistance Process a refund 12. Cancellations, Penalties & Refunds Partially refund a hotel night/service 13. Financial Adjustments Protect or recall commission 14. Commission Offer goodwill or a future travel credit 16. Goodwill & Service Recovery Answer a TSP question 17. Trip Protection Hotel says the VCC is missing/declining 15. VCC / Hotel Payment Support Hotel charged the traveler directly 15. VCC / Hotel Payment Support Build or extend an in-travel component 18. CAD & Manual Components Work a Group issue 19. Groups Escalate a Preferred supplier 20. Supplier / Product Escalation Move a case to Post-Travel 21. Post-Travel Get a supervisor involved 22. Leadership Escalations Know what to put in notes 23. Documentation Route a Finance question 24. Finance Operations Routing"}]},{"id":"2","number":"2","title":"CS Role, Ownership & Work Priority","fullTitle":"2. CS Role, Ownership & Work Priority","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ROLE</span> Customer Service is the operational support team for issues that occur during travel and for service-recovery work that requires active coordination with advisors, travelers, suppliers, Finance, air support, Groups, Product Development, or leadership. CS should own the problem until it is resolved, intentionally handed off, or escalated to the correct owner.</div>","introText":"ROLE Customer Service is the operational support team for issues that occur during travel and for service-recovery work that requires active coordination with advisors, travelers, suppliers, Finance, air support, Groups, Product Development, or leadership. CS should own the problem until it is resolved, intentionally handed off, or escalated to the correct owner.","blocks":[{"id":"2-1","heading":"2.1 Core Responsibilities","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Handle live advisor and traveler contacts for in-travel service issues.</p></li>\n<li><p>Investigate booking history, current component status, penalties, supplier responses, and prior work before acting.</p></li>\n<li><p>Coordinate hotel, transfer, air, rental-car, tour, and other in-travel changes when operationally possible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Pursue supplier waivers/refunds and resolve service failures while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Process or route refunds, financial adjustments, commission requests, agency-fee payments, and VCC issues.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use Zendesk and Plex documentation so another specialist can immediately understand the case.</p></li>\n<li><p>De-escalate difficult interactions and involve leadership when the issue exceeds agent authority, becomes abusive, or requires a management decision.</p></li>\n<li><p>Route last-day/post-travel cases to the Post-Travel process when they will take more than 24 hours to resolve.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Handle live advisor and traveler contacts for in-travel service issues. Investigate booking history, current component status, penalties, supplier responses, and prior work before acting. Coordinate hotel, transfer, air, rental-car, tour, and other in-travel changes when operationally possible. Pursue supplier waivers/refunds and resolve service failures while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible. Process or route refunds, financial adjustments, commission requests, agency-fee payments, and VCC issues. Use Zendesk and Plex documentation so another specialist can immediately understand the case. De-escalate difficult interactions and involve leadership when the issue exceeds agent authority, becomes abusive, or requires a management decision. Route last-day/post-travel cases to the Post-Travel process when they will take more than 24 hours to resolve."},{"id":"2-2","heading":"2.2 Ownership Matrix","html":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Situation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Primary owner / CS action</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Active in-travel service issue</td>\n<td>CS owns investigation and resolution.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Complex Finance/refund/VCC issue</td>\n<td>CS performs required booking work, then routes to Finance Operations as defined in this guide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preferred supplier escalation</td>\n<td>CS works supplier first; PD escalation only after threshold in Section 20.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TBO / EPS supplier escalation</td>\n<td>Use the appropriate TBO/EPS escalation channel; do not route to PD.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Air change while traveler is in travel</td>\n<td>CS coordinates with Flights/airline according to availability and operating hours.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Group issue</td>\n<td>CS assists, but Group contract/rules control; involve Groups leadership when the contract or group-specific action requires it.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Last day/post travel and &gt;24 hours to resolve</td>\n<td>Post-Travel form and handoff.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decision above agent goodwill/FTC authority</td>\n<td>CS leadership approval required.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","text":"Situation Primary owner / CS action Active in-travel service issue CS owns investigation and resolution. Complex Finance/refund/VCC issue CS performs required booking work, then routes to Finance Operations as defined in this guide. Preferred supplier escalation CS works supplier first; PD escalation only after threshold in Section 20. TBO / EPS supplier escalation Use the appropriate TBO/EPS escalation channel; do not route to PD. Air change while traveler is in travel CS coordinates with Flights/airline according to availability and operating hours. Group issue CS assists, but Group contract/rules control; involve Groups leadership when the contract or group-specific action requires it. Last day/post travel and &gt;24 hours to resolve Post-Travel form and handoff. Decision above agent goodwill/FTC authority CS leadership approval required."},{"id":"2-3","heading":"2.3 Work Priority","html":"<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Immediate traveler safety / stranded traveler / active payment failure at property.</p></li>\n<li><p>Live in-travel advisor or traveler contacts.</p></li>\n<li><p>Urgent supplier coordination that affects same-day services.</p></li>\n<li><p>Leadership escalations and callbacks within the required window.</p></li>\n<li><p>Zendesk tickets and follow-up work according to urgency and SLA.</p></li>\n<li><p>Non-urgent post-travel and administrative follow-up.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"Immediate traveler safety / stranded traveler / active payment failure at property. Live in-travel advisor or traveler contacts. Urgent supplier coordination that affects same-day services. Leadership escalations and callbacks within the required window. Zendesk tickets and follow-up work according to urgency and SLA. Non-urgent post-travel and administrative follow-up."}]},{"id":"3","number":"3","title":"Universal CS Processing Standard","fullTitle":"3. Universal CS Processing Standard","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">THE CS LOOP</span> REVIEW → DEFINE → INVESTIGATE → EXPLAIN → ACT → DOCUMENT → FOLLOW THROUGH. Do not begin by changing the booking. Begin by understanding what happened, what is still active, what is in penalty, what has already been promised, and what the traveler needs now.</div>","introText":"THE CS LOOP REVIEW → DEFINE → INVESTIGATE → EXPLAIN → ACT → DOCUMENT → FOLLOW THROUGH. Do not begin by changing the booking. Begin by understanding what happened, what is still active, what is in penalty, what has already been promised, and what the traveler needs now.","blocks":[{"id":"3-1","heading":"3.1 Seven-Step Standard","html":"<ol>\n<li><p>Review the booking: travel dates, components, status, TSP, payments, commission, remarks, mod history, supplier information, and recent notes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Define the actual problem: service failure, preference change, booking error, supplier issue, airline disruption, cancellation, refund, payment problem, complaint, or compensation request.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify downstream impact: a flight change may affect transfers; a hotel move may affect transfers, tours, dining, car rental, or commission; a cancellation may affect TSP and refund processing.</p></li>\n<li><p>Investigate before promising: contact the supplier/appropriate internal team, verify penalties and availability, and obtain approval where needed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Explain the option and financial impact clearly. Gain advisor/traveler agreement before committing a new cost or irreversible change.</p></li>\n<li><p>Complete the booking/system work and any required internal queue/form/email.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the outcome and set the next follow-up. Do not close the case simply because an email was sent.</p></li>\n</ol><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">NO-PROMISE RULE</span> Never guarantee a supplier waiver, insurance reimbursement, refund approval, room upgrade, compensation, or leadership outcome before the responsible party has approved it.</div>","text":"Review the booking: travel dates, components, status, TSP, payments, commission, remarks, mod history, supplier information, and recent notes. Define the actual problem: service failure, preference change, booking error, supplier issue, airline disruption, cancellation, refund, payment problem, complaint, or compensation request. Identify downstream impact: a flight change may affect transfers; a hotel move may affect transfers, tours, dining, car rental, or commission; a cancellation may affect TSP and refund processing. Investigate before promising: contact the supplier/appropriate internal team, verify penalties and availability, and obtain approval where needed. Explain the option and financial impact clearly. Gain advisor/traveler agreement before committing a new cost or irreversible change. Complete the booking/system work and any required internal queue/form/email. Document the outcome and set the next follow-up. Do not close the case simply because an email was sent. NO-PROMISE RULE Never guarantee a supplier waiver, insurance reimbursement, refund approval, room upgrade, compensation, or leadership outcome before the responsible party has approved it."},{"id":"3-2","heading":"3.2 Before Touching the Booking","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Confirm the caller/booking relationship and current travel status.</p></li>\n<li><p>Read the latest notes first, especially anything that began in travel.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify whether the component is already consumed, partially consumed, in penalty, or still changeable.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check TSP details rather than assuming coverage.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check whether commission protection/goodwill has already been used on the booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check source/type: Preferred, TBO, EPS/Affiliate, CAD, Group, direct supplier.</p></li>\n<li><p>Look for prior supplier communication and promises.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Confirm the caller/booking relationship and current travel status. Read the latest notes first, especially anything that began in travel. Verify whether the component is already consumed, partially consumed, in penalty, or still changeable. Check TSP details rather than assuming coverage. Check whether commission protection/goodwill has already been used on the booking. Check source/type: Preferred, TBO, EPS/Affiliate, CAD, Group, direct supplier. Look for prior supplier communication and promises."},{"id":"3-3","heading":"3.3 When the SOP Does Not Fit Cleanly","html":"<p>Use this when a procedure does not clearly cover the situation in front of you:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Identify exactly what is unclear: policy, penalty, ownership, supplier response, system behavior, or financial authority.</p></li>\n<li><p>Separate what is confirmed from what is assumed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check the source that controls the issue: booking terms, supplier confirmation, TSP terms, Group contract, current airline record, or internal owner.</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not commit an irreversible action while a material fact is still unknown.</p></li>\n<li><p>Resolve what can be resolved now.</p></li>\n<li><p>Escalate only the specific decision or exception that remains.</p></li>\n<li><p>Tell the advisor/traveler what is confirmed, what is pending, and what happens next.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"Use this when a procedure does not clearly cover the situation in front of you: Identify exactly what is unclear: policy, penalty, ownership, supplier response, system behavior, or financial authority. Separate what is confirmed from what is assumed. Check the source that controls the issue: booking terms, supplier confirmation, TSP terms, Group contract, current airline record, or internal owner. Do not commit an irreversible action while a material fact is still unknown. Resolve what can be resolved now. Escalate only the specific decision or exception that remains. Tell the advisor/traveler what is confirmed, what is pending, and what happens next."}]}]},{"id":"plex-booking-review","label":"Plex & Booking Review","items":[{"id":"4","number":"4","title":"Plex Operating Rules & Booking Review","fullTitle":"4. Plex Operating Rules & Booking Review","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Plex is the operational record. Read history before adding new remarks or making financial changes. Mod history, internal communications, component details, commission, and notes should be used together when reconstructing what occurred.</div>","introText":"RULE Plex is the operational record. Read history before adding new remarks or making financial changes. Mod history, internal communications, component details, commission, and notes should be used together when reconstructing what occurred.","blocks":[{"id":"4-1","heading":"4.1 Booking Review Order","html":"<ol>\n<li><p>Confirm dates and whether the traveler is pre-travel, in travel, on the last day, or post-travel.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review booking summary and active components.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review recent Other History/remarks, especially entries from the start of travel.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review component details: status, supplier, confirmation, penalties, room/transfer/air details.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review TSP and applicable terms if protection is relevant.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review commission and prior adjustments if money will change.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use mod history when investigation requires understanding what changed and when.</p></li>\n</ol><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">DOCUMENTATION STANDARD</span> Another specialist should be able to open the booking and understand the issue, what was verified, who was contacted, what was approved/declined, the financial impact, what the advisor/traveler accepted, and what still needs to happen.</div>","text":"Confirm dates and whether the traveler is pre-travel, in travel, on the last day, or post-travel. Review booking summary and active components. Review recent Other History/remarks, especially entries from the start of travel. Review component details: status, supplier, confirmation, penalties, room/transfer/air details. Review TSP and applicable terms if protection is relevant. Review commission and prior adjustments if money will change. Use mod history when investigation requires understanding what changed and when. DOCUMENTATION STANDARD Another specialist should be able to open the booking and understand the issue, what was verified, who was contacted, what was approved/declined, the financial impact, what the advisor/traveler accepted, and what still needs to happen."},{"id":"4-2","heading":"4.2 In-Travel Changes and Plex Limitations","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Some in-travel flight changes may not import back into Plex. When this occurs, the airline website using the record locator may show the current flight information more accurately.</p></li>\n<li><p>Land Amend is generally not the preferred in-travel path because components may already be in penalty and supplier communication is still required. If a later component is not in penalty and a date is changed, communicate the change directly to the vendor.</p></li>\n<li><p>CS generally works from FIT and CAD/competitive hotel areas relevant to the actual booking; do not use unrelated tabs simply because they are available.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Some in-travel flight changes may not import back into Plex. When this occurs, the airline website using the record locator may show the current flight information more accurately. Land Amend is generally not the preferred in-travel path because components may already be in penalty and supplier communication is still required. If a later component is not in penalty and a date is changed, communicate the change directly to the vendor. CS generally works from FIT and CAD/competitive hotel areas relevant to the actual booking; do not use unrelated tabs simply because they are available."}]},{"id":"5","number":"5","title":"Pre-Travel vs. In-Travel Rules","fullTitle":"5. Pre-Travel vs. In-Travel Rules","introHtml":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Topic</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Pre-Travel</strong></th>\n<th><strong>In-Travel</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Updated itinerary</td>\n<td>Send after booking changes so the advisor has a record of what changed.</td>\n<td>Use judgment based on the change. For air, current airline record may be more accurate when Plex does not re-import the change.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Penalties</td>\n<td>Normal modification/cancellation rules apply.</td>\n<td>Assume penalties may already apply until verified; supplier contact is often required.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Agency/Planning Fee</td>\n<td>Can be added according to standard pre-travel process.</td>\n<td>Cannot be added by itself. There must be a booking modification that requires payment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hotel nightly refund</td>\n<td>Use the normal booking/rate calculation.</td>\n<td>For approved partial hotel-night refunds, use the average nightly rate of the affected hotel line item.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Land Amend</td>\n<td>Normal servicing tool where appropriate.</td>\n<td>Generally avoid as a default; communicate directly with vendor for any in-travel change.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Service recovery</td>\n<td>Primarily prevention/correction.</td>\n<td>Resolve while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">WHY THIS MATTERS</span> In-travel handling is not simply pre-travel servicing performed later. Services may be partially consumed, penalties may already be active, suppliers may need to intervene immediately, and downstream components can be affected.</div>","introText":"Topic Pre-Travel In-Travel Updated itinerary Send after booking changes so the advisor has a record of what changed. Use judgment based on the change. For air, current airline record may be more accurate when Plex does not re-import the change. Penalties Normal modification/cancellation rules apply. Assume penalties may already apply until verified; supplier contact is often required. Agency/Planning Fee Can be added according to standard pre-travel process. Cannot be added by itself. There must be a booking modification that requires payment. Hotel nightly refund Use the normal booking/rate calculation. For approved partial hotel-night refunds, use the average nightly rate of the affected hotel line item. Land Amend Normal servicing tool where appropriate. Generally avoid as a default; communicate directly with vendor for any in-travel change. Service recovery Primarily prevention/correction. Resolve while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible. WHY THIS MATTERS In-travel handling is not simply pre-travel servicing performed later. Services may be partially consumed, penalties may already be active, suppliers may need to intervene immediately, and downstream components can be affected.","blocks":[]}]},{"id":"advisor-interaction","label":"Traveler Interaction & De-escalation","items":[{"id":"6","number":"6","title":"Advisor / Traveler Interaction & De-escalation","fullTitle":"6. Advisor / Traveler Interaction & De-escalation","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Empathy does not mean promising compensation. Acknowledge the impact, explain what you can do now, and keep control of the resolution path.</div>","introText":"RULE Empathy does not mean promising compensation. Acknowledge the impact, explain what you can do now, and keep control of the resolution path.","blocks":[{"id":"6-1","heading":"6.1 Interaction Standard","html":"<ol>\n<li><p>Listen for the actual requested outcome.</p></li>\n<li><p>Acknowledge the impact without assigning blame before investigating.</p></li>\n<li><p>Summarize the issue back to the caller.</p></li>\n<li><p>Set the next action: “I am going to contact the property/vendor/air team and verify the available options.”</p></li>\n<li><p>Explain financial or timing limitations before the caller commits to a change.</p></li>\n<li><p>Give realistic follow-up expectations.</p></li>\n<li><p>Close the loop with a recap of what was done and what happens next.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"Listen for the actual requested outcome. Acknowledge the impact without assigning blame before investigating. Summarize the issue back to the caller. Set the next action: “I am going to contact the property/vendor/air team and verify the available options.” Explain financial or timing limitations before the caller commits to a change. Give realistic follow-up expectations. Close the loop with a recap of what was done and what happens next."},{"id":"6-2","heading":"6.2 De-escalation","html":"<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Do:</strong> stay calm, use concise language, acknowledge frustration, separate the emotion from the operational issue, and offer the next concrete step.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Do not:</strong> argue, mirror the caller’s tone, blame another department, or use “policy says no” as the entire explanation.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>If the caller remains abusive:</strong> after reasonable de-escalation attempts, contact leadership and advise that a supervisor will become involved.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">LEADERSHIP CALLBACK</span> Urgent/in-travel: leadership may take the call immediately if on duty and available; otherwise callback within 1 hour. Non-urgent and post-travel escalations: callback within 24 hours.</div>","text":"Do: stay calm, use concise language, acknowledge frustration, separate the emotion from the operational issue, and offer the next concrete step. Do not: argue, mirror the caller’s tone, blame another department, or use “policy says no” as the entire explanation. If the caller remains abusive: after reasonable de-escalation attempts, contact leadership and advise that a supervisor will become involved. LEADERSHIP CALLBACK Urgent/in-travel: leadership may take the call immediately if on duty and available; otherwise callback within 1 hour. Non-urgent and post-travel escalations: callback within 24 hours."},{"id":"6-3","heading":"6.3 Message Frameworks","html":"<p>These are frameworks to adapt, not scripts to read verbatim — the goal is knowing how to construct the message for the situation, not memorizing exact wording.</p>\n<p><strong>Pending supplier</strong></p>\n<p>\"We have contacted [supplier] to confirm [specific item]. We do not have final approval yet, so I do not want to overstate the outcome. We will follow up once we receive their response.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Refund pending</strong></p>\n<p>\"The refund has been submitted for [amount]. Current processing time is 7–10 business days. [Commission impact, if applicable.]\"</p>\n<p><strong>Cancellation under review</strong></p>\n<p>\"Before we finalize the cancellation, we are confirming the applicable penalty and refund position so we can give you the correct financial impact.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Internal team pending</strong></p>\n<p>\"I have sent this to [team] for [specific action]. The case remains open while we wait for that response, and we will continue from there.\"</p>\n<p><strong>No approval yet</strong></p>\n<p>\"I can confirm [known fact]. I cannot yet confirm [waiver/refund/compensation/change] until [supplier/internal owner] approves it.\"</p>","text":"These are frameworks to adapt, not scripts to read verbatim — the goal is knowing how to construct the message for the situation, not memorizing exact wording. Pending supplier \"We have contacted [supplier] to confirm [specific item]. We do not have final approval yet, so I do not want to overstate the outcome. We will follow up once we receive their response.\" Refund pending \"The refund has been submitted for [amount]. Current processing time is 7–10 business days. [Commission impact, if applicable.]\" Cancellation under review \"Before we finalize the cancellation, we are confirming the applicable penalty and refund position so we can give you the correct financial impact.\" Internal team pending \"I have sent this to [team] for [specific action]. The case remains open while we wait for that response, and we will continue from there.\" No approval yet \"I can confirm [known fact]. I cannot yet confirm [waiver/refund/compensation/change] until [supplier/internal owner] approves it.\""}]}]},{"id":"zendesk","label":"Zendesk: Ticket Handling","items":[{"id":"7","number":"7","title":"Zendesk: Ticket Handling End to End","fullTitle":"7. Zendesk: Ticket Handling End to End","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> A Zendesk ticket is not complete because an email was sent. It is complete when the requested work is resolved, intentionally waiting on an external party with the correct status/follow-up, or handed to the correct owner with clear documentation.</div>","introText":"RULE A Zendesk ticket is not complete because an email was sent. It is complete when the requested work is resolved, intentionally waiting on an external party with the correct status/follow-up, or handed to the correct owner with clear documentation.","blocks":[{"id":"7-1","heading":"7.1 Work a CS Ticket","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Read the full ticket thread and the Plex booking before replying or taking action.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Any email/ticket assigned to CS.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Open the ticket and identify booking number, traveler, travel status, urgency, and ask.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review recent Plex notes and prior ticket history.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Assign/own the ticket while you are actively working it.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use internal notes for internal-only information; use the customer-facing response for advisor/traveler communication.</p></li>\n<li><p>Contact suppliers/internal partners as required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Set the ticket to the status that matches the actual work state; do not mark solved while required action is still outstanding.</p></li>\n<li><p>Record meaningful phone/supplier outcomes in Plex when they affect the booking.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Waiting on supplier/internal party</td>\n<td>Keep a clear follow-up date/status rather than solving.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Work transferred to another owner</td>\n<td>Document the handoff and reason.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Resolved</td>\n<td>Send a concise recap and ensure Plex reflects the outcome.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Issue/ask, investigation, contacts, response, financial impact, next action, owner.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> The ticket involves a live traveler, high financial exposure, legal/safety risk, payment failure, or decision outside authority.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> The advisor/traveler has the answer or confirmed resolution, required system work is complete, and no unowned follow-up remains.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Read the full ticket thread and the Plex booking before replying or taking action. Use when: Any email/ticket assigned to CS. Before you start Open the ticket and identify booking number, traveler, travel status, urgency, and ask. Review recent Plex notes and prior ticket history. Steps Assign/own the ticket while you are actively working it. Use internal notes for internal-only information; use the customer-facing response for advisor/traveler communication. Contact suppliers/internal partners as required. Set the ticket to the status that matches the actual work state; do not mark solved while required action is still outstanding. Record meaningful phone/supplier outcomes in Plex when they affect the booking. If / Then If Then Waiting on supplier/internal party Keep a clear follow-up date/status rather than solving. Work transferred to another owner Document the handoff and reason. Resolved Send a concise recap and ensure Plex reflects the outcome. Document Issue/ask, investigation, contacts, response, financial impact, next action, owner. ESCALATE WHEN The ticket involves a live traveler, high financial exposure, legal/safety risk, payment failure, or decision outside authority. COMPLETE WHEN The advisor/traveler has the answer or confirmed resolution, required system work is complete, and no unowned follow-up remains."},{"id":"7-2","heading":"7.2 Who Owns the Next Action?","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">OWNERSHIP RULE</span> A dependency is not the same as completion. Do not solve a ticket simply because another team, supplier, or traveler now needs to respond. Solve only when the request is complete or ownership has been intentionally transferred with no remaining CS responsibility.</div>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 25%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 25%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 25%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 25%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Situation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Who owns next action?</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Zendesk status</strong></th>\n<th><strong>What CS should do</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>CS still researching or taking action</td><td>CS</td><td>Open / Researching</td><td>Continue working and document next step</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting on advisor/client information</td><td>Advisor / requester</td><td>Waiting on TA/Requester</td><td>Tell them exactly what is needed and why</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting on hotel, DMC, transfer vendor, or supplier</td><td>External supplier</td><td>Waiting on Vendor</td><td>Document who was contacted, what is pending, and follow-up timing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Waiting on Finance, Flights, Product, Groups, or another Classic team</td><td>Internal Classic team</td><td>Waiting on Internal CV Response</td><td>Document the internal request and keep ownership visible until response/handoff is complete</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Supervisor/leadership decision required</td><td>Leadership</td><td>Escalated</td><td>Include the decision needed, facts, financial exposure, and your recommendation</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Work intentionally transferred to another team that has fully accepted ownership</td><td>Receiving team</td><td>Reassign + Open as appropriate</td><td>Document handoff and confirm there is no remaining CS action</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Everything requested is complete and no follow-up remains</td><td>None</td><td>Solved</td><td>Send final recap and ensure Plex notes are complete</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","text":"OWNERSHIP RULE A dependency is not the same as completion. Do not solve a ticket simply because another team, supplier, or traveler now needs to respond. Solve only when the request is complete or ownership has been intentionally transferred with no remaining CS responsibility. Situation Who owns next action? Zendesk status What CS should do CS still researching or taking action CS Open / Researching Continue working and document next step Waiting on advisor/client information Advisor / requester Waiting on TA/Requester Tell them exactly what is needed and why Waiting on hotel, DMC, transfer vendor, or supplier External supplier Waiting on Vendor Document who was contacted, what is pending, and follow-up timing Waiting on Finance, Flights, Product, Groups, or another Classic team Internal Classic team Waiting on Internal CV Response Document the internal request and keep ownership visible until response/handoff is complete Supervisor/leadership decision required Leadership Escalated Include the decision needed, facts, financial exposure, and your recommendation Work intentionally transferred to another team that has fully accepted ownership Receiving team Reassign + Open as appropriate Document handoff and confirm there is no remaining CS action Everything requested is complete and no follow-up remains None Solved Send final recap and ensure Plex notes are complete"},{"id":"7-3","heading":"7.3 Chat Inactivity Closeout","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Follow the standard inactivity timing before ending a chat session rather than ending it immediately or leaving it open indefinitely.</div>\n<p><strong>Steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>After 2 minutes with no response, send a follow-up message checking whether the traveler/advisor is still there.</p></li>\n<li><p>Wait an additional 2 minutes.</p></li>\n<li><p>If there is still no response, let them know they are welcome to reconnect if they still need help, then end the session.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the closeout the same as any other chat/ticket interaction.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"POLICY / RULE Follow the standard inactivity timing before ending a chat session rather than ending it immediately or leaving it open indefinitely. Steps After 2 minutes with no response, send a follow-up message checking whether the traveler/advisor is still there. Wait an additional 2 minutes. If there is still no response, let them know they are welcome to reconnect if they still need help, then end the session. Document the closeout the same as any other chat/ticket interaction."}]}]},{"id":"hotel-transfers-air","label":"Hotel, Transfers & Air Disruptions","items":[{"id":"8","number":"8","title":"Hotel In-Travel Assistance","fullTitle":"8. Hotel In-Travel Assistance","introHtml":"","introText":"","blocks":[{"id":"8-1","heading":"8.1 Traveler Wants to Leave / Change Hotels","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not cancel the original hotel or promise a refund until penalties, supplier position, TSP, replacement availability, and traveler financial exposure are understood.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Traveler wants to leave early, relocate, shorten stay, or move because of dissatisfaction/service failure.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Read the hotel confirmation, room type, requests/guarantees, penalty terms, TSP, and recent notes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Determine whether the issue is a service failure, health/safety concern, or preference.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify whether the guest has already spoken with property management and what the hotel offered.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact the hotel/vendor and attempt an in-house resolution first when appropriate.</p></li>\n<li><p>Ask for the exact supplier position on unused nights and any waiver/refund.</p></li>\n<li><p>If relocation is necessary, price/secure an appropriate alternative before releasing the original space when possible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Explain any penalty/new cost before obtaining approval.</p></li>\n<li><p>Coordinate downstream transfers/tours/car/air if the hotel move changes logistics.</p></li>\n<li><p>Process approved financial adjustments/refunds and commission impact.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>No TSP and supplier denies waiver</td>\n<td>Traveler may remain liable for the original hotel and the cost of a new hotel.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TSP is present</td>\n<td>Check the specific plan/terms. Still pursue supplier waiver where applicable; do not promise insurance reimbursement.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Issue can be corrected in-house</td>\n<td>Give the property an opportunity to resolve while traveler is there.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immediate safety/health concern</td>\n<td>Prioritize moving the traveler to safety and escalate leadership as needed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Complaint details, room/service issue, hotel contacts, hotel response, options offered, traveler decision, financial impact, new confirmations, follow-up.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Traveler safety is at risk; replacement cost exceeds authority; supplier refuses a reasonable resolution on a Preferred product; high-value/VIP case requires management judgment.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Traveler has a safe confirmed accommodation, original hotel disposition is known, related components are updated, financial action is complete/routed, and all parties have been advised.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not cancel the original hotel or promise a refund until penalties, supplier position, TSP, replacement availability, and traveler financial exposure are understood. Use when: Traveler wants to leave early, relocate, shorten stay, or move because of dissatisfaction/service failure. Before you start Read the hotel confirmation, room type, requests/guarantees, penalty terms, TSP, and recent notes. Determine whether the issue is a service failure, health/safety concern, or preference. Identify whether the guest has already spoken with property management and what the hotel offered. Steps Contact the hotel/vendor and attempt an in-house resolution first when appropriate. Ask for the exact supplier position on unused nights and any waiver/refund. If relocation is necessary, price/secure an appropriate alternative before releasing the original space when possible. Explain any penalty/new cost before obtaining approval. Coordinate downstream transfers/tours/car/air if the hotel move changes logistics. Process approved financial adjustments/refunds and commission impact. If / Then If Then No TSP and supplier denies waiver Traveler may remain liable for the original hotel and the cost of a new hotel. TSP is present Check the specific plan/terms. Still pursue supplier waiver where applicable; do not promise insurance reimbursement. Issue can be corrected in-house Give the property an opportunity to resolve while traveler is there. Immediate safety/health concern Prioritize moving the traveler to safety and escalate leadership as needed. Document Complaint details, room/service issue, hotel contacts, hotel response, options offered, traveler decision, financial impact, new confirmations, follow-up. ESCALATE WHEN Traveler safety is at risk; replacement cost exceeds authority; supplier refuses a reasonable resolution on a Preferred product; high-value/VIP case requires management judgment. COMPLETE WHEN Traveler has a safe confirmed accommodation, original hotel disposition is known, related components are updated, financial action is complete/routed, and all parties have been advised."},{"id":"8-2","heading":"8.2 Bedding / Connecting Room / Request Not Honored","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> A request that was never guaranteed is not automatically a compensable service failure. CS should still attempt to improve the situation and assess the practical impact.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Bedding, connecting rooms, floor/location, view, or similar request is not provided.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Verify whether the item was guaranteed or only requested.</p></li>\n<li><p>Read supplier comments/booking documentation.</p></li>\n<li><p>For Group bookings, do not treat the bedding displayed in Groups Manager as proof that bedding was guaranteed. The Bedding field represents the request on file.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify the actual room category and what bedding configurations that category supports before determining whether there was a supplier failure.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact the property and ask what can be done now.</p></li>\n<li><p>Seek room move/alternative configuration if available.</p></li>\n<li><p>Explain clearly if the booking documents only showed a request subject to availability.</p></li>\n<li><p>Evaluate unusual impact separately (for example, minor children separated from parents).</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Whether guaranteed/requested, property response, alternatives, traveler acceptance/refusal.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> The operational impact creates a safety concern or a reasonable solution is not available.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> The property has addressed the request or the traveler has been given the verified options and expectations.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE A request that was never guaranteed is not automatically a compensable service failure. CS should still attempt to improve the situation and assess the practical impact. Use when: Bedding, connecting rooms, floor/location, view, or similar request is not provided. Before you start Verify whether the item was guaranteed or only requested. Read supplier comments/booking documentation. For Group bookings, do not treat the bedding displayed in Groups Manager as proof that bedding was guaranteed. The Bedding field represents the request on file. Verify the actual room category and what bedding configurations that category supports before determining whether there was a supplier failure. Steps Contact the property and ask what can be done now. Seek room move/alternative configuration if available. Explain clearly if the booking documents only showed a request subject to availability. Evaluate unusual impact separately (for example, minor children separated from parents). Document Whether guaranteed/requested, property response, alternatives, traveler acceptance/refusal. ESCALATE WHEN The operational impact creates a safety concern or a reasonable solution is not available. COMPLETE WHEN The property has addressed the request or the traveler has been given the verified options and expectations."},{"id":"8-3","heading":"8.3 Hotel Service Failure / Complaint","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Solve the service issue first; compensation is secondary. Work the property while the traveler is still in-house whenever possible.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Room condition, cleanliness, construction/renovation, amenity failure, service complaint, or other hotel issue.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Read notes carefully; distinguish facts from assumptions.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify what was represented at booking and what is actually occurring.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact hotel management, not only front desk when escalation is needed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Ask what corrective action can happen now: room move, maintenance, housekeeping, amenity restoration, credit, meal, etc.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the proposed solution is inadequate, build the next-best option and determine whether leadership/PD involvement is needed.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Objective complaint facts, what property confirmed, corrective action, compensation offered, traveler response.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Preferred supplier becomes unresponsive for 72 hours after complaint receipt or proposed solution does not align with CV standard; or immediate traveler impact requires leadership sooner.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Traveler has a workable resolution and all compensation/financial adjustments are documented.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Solve the service issue first; compensation is secondary. Work the property while the traveler is still in-house whenever possible. Use when: Room condition, cleanliness, construction/renovation, amenity failure, service complaint, or other hotel issue. Before you start Read notes carefully; distinguish facts from assumptions. Verify what was represented at booking and what is actually occurring. Steps Contact hotel management, not only front desk when escalation is needed. Ask what corrective action can happen now: room move, maintenance, housekeeping, amenity restoration, credit, meal, etc. If the proposed solution is inadequate, build the next-best option and determine whether leadership/PD involvement is needed. Document Objective complaint facts, what property confirmed, corrective action, compensation offered, traveler response. ESCALATE WHEN Preferred supplier becomes unresponsive for 72 hours after complaint receipt or proposed solution does not align with CV standard; or immediate traveler impact requires leadership sooner. COMPLETE WHEN Traveler has a workable resolution and all compensation/financial adjustments are documented."},{"id":"8-4","heading":"8.4 Consortia / Preferred Amenity Not Received","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Agency consortium membership or hotel participation alone does not prove that a specific booking qualifies for an amenity.</div>\n<p>Before treating a missing amenity as a supplier failure:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Confirm the agency/consortium information.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm the hotel participates in the applicable program.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm the booked rate plan and room category qualify.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review the booking documentation for the specific amenity.</p></li>\n<li><p>Contact the hotel when eligibility or fulfillment remains unclear.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Do not promise compensation solely because the advisor or traveler believes the booking should have included a consortium benefit.</p>","text":"POLICY / RULE Agency consortium membership or hotel participation alone does not prove that a specific booking qualifies for an amenity. Before treating a missing amenity as a supplier failure: Confirm the agency/consortium information. Confirm the hotel participates in the applicable program. Confirm the booked rate plan and room category qualify. Review the booking documentation for the specific amenity. Contact the hotel when eligibility or fulfillment remains unclear. Do not promise compensation solely because the advisor or traveler believes the booking should have included a consortium benefit."},{"id":"8-5","heading":"8.5 Extra-Person Charge at Hotel","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not automatically classify an extra-person charge collected by the hotel as an error.</div>\n<p>Some hotel/rate programs may price the Classic booking based on standard or double occupancy while requiring additional-person charges to be paid directly at the property.</p>\n<p>When a traveler questions an extra-person charge:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Review the booking instructions and room occupancy.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm what was included in the Classic sell price.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify any direct-pay additional-person policy.</p></li>\n<li><p>Contact the hotel/vendor if the booking documents and hotel charge conflict.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Escalate only after confirming that the hotel is charging something inconsistent with the booked terms.</p>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not automatically classify an extra-person charge collected by the hotel as an error. Some hotel/rate programs may price the Classic booking based on standard or double occupancy while requiring additional-person charges to be paid directly at the property. When a traveler questions an extra-person charge: Review the booking instructions and room occupancy. Confirm what was included in the Classic sell price. Verify any direct-pay additional-person policy. Contact the hotel/vendor if the booking documents and hotel charge conflict. Escalate only after confirming that the hotel is charging something inconsistent with the booked terms."}]},{"id":"9","number":"9","title":"Transfers & Ground Transportation","fullTitle":"9. Transfers & Ground Transportation","introHtml":"","introText":"","blocks":[{"id":"9-1","heading":"9.1 Transfer Problem / Missed Pickup","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Investigate before refunding or escalating. Verify flight timing, pickup instructions, traveler actions, vendor records, and local operating practice.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Driver not found, missed pickup, late transfer, wrong pickup time, or transfer service failure.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Review manifest/transfer confirmation, flight details, emergency contact instructions, and notes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm whether the traveler is still waiting, already took alternate transport, or missed the service.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact the transfer vendor/emergency line.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify driver dispatch, meeting point, wait time, flight delay status, and any contact attempts.</p></li>\n<li><p>Arrange immediate alternate transportation if required and authorized.</p></li>\n<li><p>Determine supplier refund/penalty responsibility after the traveler is moving safely.</p></li>\n<li><p>Update downstream pickup details if the traveler’s flight/hotel changed.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Flight changed</td>\n<td>Reconfirm the transfer against the new flight; do not assume the vendor received the change.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traveler used a taxi/alternate transport</td>\n<td>Keep receipts/documentation if reimbursement will be reviewed; do not promise reimbursement before approval.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Driver details not provided</td>\n<td>Check destination/vendor practice; driver details are more commonly sent in some destinations (training specifically referenced Europe/Japan), but absence alone is not proof of failure.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Flight/pickup facts, vendor contact, driver status, alternate transport, receipts if applicable, refund position, next action.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Traveler is stranded, vendor is unreachable, replacement requires significant out-of-pocket cost, or repeated supplier failure requires escalation.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Traveler has transportation, future pickups are corrected, and the financial/supplier issue is resolved or actively owned.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Investigate before refunding or escalating. Verify flight timing, pickup instructions, traveler actions, vendor records, and local operating practice. Use when: Driver not found, missed pickup, late transfer, wrong pickup time, or transfer service failure. Before you start Review manifest/transfer confirmation, flight details, emergency contact instructions, and notes. Confirm whether the traveler is still waiting, already took alternate transport, or missed the service. Steps Contact the transfer vendor/emergency line. Verify driver dispatch, meeting point, wait time, flight delay status, and any contact attempts. Arrange immediate alternate transportation if required and authorized. Determine supplier refund/penalty responsibility after the traveler is moving safely. Update downstream pickup details if the traveler’s flight/hotel changed. If / Then If Then Flight changed Reconfirm the transfer against the new flight; do not assume the vendor received the change. Traveler used a taxi/alternate transport Keep receipts/documentation if reimbursement will be reviewed; do not promise reimbursement before approval. Driver details not provided Check destination/vendor practice; driver details are more commonly sent in some destinations (training specifically referenced Europe/Japan), but absence alone is not proof of failure. Document Flight/pickup facts, vendor contact, driver status, alternate transport, receipts if applicable, refund position, next action. ESCALATE WHEN Traveler is stranded, vendor is unreachable, replacement requires significant out-of-pocket cost, or repeated supplier failure requires escalation. COMPLETE WHEN Traveler has transportation, future pickups are corrected, and the financial/supplier issue is resolved or actively owned."},{"id":"9-2","heading":"9.2 Transfer Change After Flight Change","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> A flight change creates a transfer-review obligation. Reconfirm any affected airport transfer rather than assuming it updated automatically.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Arrival/departure flight changes while a transfer is booked.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Verify new flight number/date/time and current transfer status.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact transfer vendor with new flight details.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm revised pickup time/meeting instructions.</p></li>\n<li><p>Update Plex/notes and advise traveler/advisor.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>New flight, vendor confirmation, revised transfer details.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Vendor cannot accommodate and traveler is in travel.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> New transfer arrangement is confirmed and communicated.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE A flight change creates a transfer-review obligation. Reconfirm any affected airport transfer rather than assuming it updated automatically. Use when: Arrival/departure flight changes while a transfer is booked. Before you start Verify new flight number/date/time and current transfer status. Steps Contact transfer vendor with new flight details. Confirm revised pickup time/meeting instructions. Update Plex/notes and advise traveler/advisor. Document New flight, vendor confirmation, revised transfer details. ESCALATE WHEN Vendor cannot accommodate and traveler is in travel. COMPLETE WHEN New transfer arrangement is confirmed and communicated."}]},{"id":"10","number":"10","title":"Air Disruptions & In-Travel Flight Support","fullTitle":"10. Air Disruptions & In-Travel Flight Support","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Treat an air change as a trip change, not just a flight change. Review every downstream component that depends on arrival/departure timing.</div>","introText":"RULE Treat an air change as a trip change, not just a flight change. Review every downstream component that depends on arrival/departure timing.","blocks":[{"id":"10-1","heading":"10.1 In-Travel Flight Change / Disruption","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Verify the current airline record, coordinate with Flights/airline, and review downstream trip impact before closing the case.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Schedule change, cancellation, misconnection, same-day change, or traveler needs air assistance during travel.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Open air details/record locator and review recent notes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check Flights availability/operating hours and whether airline contact is required.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Determine the airline’s current confirmed itinerary.</p></li>\n<li><p>If Flights is available, use the internal air-support path; if closed and immediate action is required, contact the airline as trained/authorized.</p></li>\n<li><p>Recheck airport transfers, hotel arrival, tours, rental car, and any other timed component.</p></li>\n<li><p>Advise traveler to use the airline record locator/website for current air information if Plex does not reflect the in-travel modification.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Flight change does not re-import to Plex</td>\n<td>Document the verified airline itinerary and explain where the traveler can see the live record.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Misconnection changes arrival day</td>\n<td>Review hotel no-show risk and transfer cancellation/rebooking immediately.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Airline-controlled issue</td>\n<td>Do not promise airline compensation; focus on confirmed re-accommodation and trip impact.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>New flight details, who changed it, airline/Flights contact, downstream actions, traveler/advisor advisement.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Traveler is stranded without viable airline option, significant additional cost is requested from Classic, or air issue creates hotel/group penalties needing leadership judgment.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Current flight is confirmed and all affected land components have been reviewed/updated.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Verify the current airline record, coordinate with Flights/airline, and review downstream trip impact before closing the case. Use when: Schedule change, cancellation, misconnection, same-day change, or traveler needs air assistance during travel. Before you start Open air details/record locator and review recent notes. Check Flights availability/operating hours and whether airline contact is required. Steps Determine the airline’s current confirmed itinerary. If Flights is available, use the internal air-support path; if closed and immediate action is required, contact the airline as trained/authorized. Recheck airport transfers, hotel arrival, tours, rental car, and any other timed component. Advise traveler to use the airline record locator/website for current air information if Plex does not reflect the in-travel modification. If / Then If Then Flight change does not re-import to Plex Document the verified airline itinerary and explain where the traveler can see the live record. Misconnection changes arrival day Review hotel no-show risk and transfer cancellation/rebooking immediately. Airline-controlled issue Do not promise airline compensation; focus on confirmed re-accommodation and trip impact. Document New flight details, who changed it, airline/Flights contact, downstream actions, traveler/advisor advisement. ESCALATE WHEN Traveler is stranded without viable airline option, significant additional cost is requested from Classic, or air issue creates hotel/group penalties needing leadership judgment. COMPLETE WHEN Current flight is confirmed and all affected land components have been reviewed/updated."}]},{"id":"11","number":"11","title":"Rental Cars, Tours & Other Components","fullTitle":"11. Rental Cars, Tours & Other Components","introHtml":"","introText":"","blocks":[{"id":"11-1","heading":"11.1 Rental Cars","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Review confirmation, pickup/drop-off dates/times, location, driver requirements, and direct-pay mandatory fees before changing a rental.</p></li>\n<li><p>Training emphasized that insurance, GPS, and certain destination/vendor fees may be paid direct; the booking documents should be used to set expectations.</p></li>\n<li><p>If a hotel move or flight change changes pickup/drop-off needs, review the car rental as part of the ripple-effect check.</p></li>\n<li><p>Seek supplier approval for unused-day refunds rather than assuming an early return will automatically refund.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Review confirmation, pickup/drop-off dates/times, location, driver requirements, and direct-pay mandatory fees before changing a rental. Training emphasized that insurance, GPS, and certain destination/vendor fees may be paid direct; the booking documents should be used to set expectations. If a hotel move or flight change changes pickup/drop-off needs, review the car rental as part of the ripple-effect check. Seek supplier approval for unused-day refunds rather than assuming an early return will automatically refund."},{"id":"11-2","heading":"11.2 Tours / Activities","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Verify cancellation deadline, pickup point, date/time, and whether a hotel move/flight change affects the activity.</p></li>\n<li><p>If an activity is missed because another component failed, document the causal chain and seek supplier waiver before promising reimbursement.</p></li>\n<li><p>When adding a service in travel, take payment as required and remember any resulting commission payout request.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RIPPLE-EFFECT CHECK</span> Any time you change air, hotel, or travel dates, scan every remaining component. A correct change on one line can still create a failed trip if the transfer, tour, car, or next hotel is left unchanged.</div>","text":"Verify cancellation deadline, pickup point, date/time, and whether a hotel move/flight change affects the activity. If an activity is missed because another component failed, document the causal chain and seek supplier waiver before promising reimbursement. When adding a service in travel, take payment as required and remember any resulting commission payout request. RIPPLE-EFFECT CHECK Any time you change air, hotel, or travel dates, scan every remaining component. A correct change on one line can still create a failed trip if the transfer, tour, car, or next hotel is left unchanged."}]}]},{"id":"cancellations-financial","label":"Cancellations, Refunds & Financial Adjustments","items":[{"id":"12","number":"12","title":"Cancellations, Penalties & Refunds","fullTitle":"12. Cancellations, Penalties & Refunds","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">REFUND SLA</span> Customer refunds: 7–10 business days. The 7–14 business-day timeframe discussed in training applies to commission payouts, not customer refunds.</div>","introText":"REFUND SLA Customer refunds: 7–10 business days. The 7–14 business-day timeframe discussed in training applies to commission payouts, not customer refunds.","blocks":[{"id":"12-1","heading":"12.1 Process a Supplier-Approved Refund","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not send a refund to Finance until the booking is financially correct and the supplier approval/refund basis is documented.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Supplier waives penalty, authorizes full/partial refund, TBO/EPS confirms refund, or Classic approves an adjustment requiring a customer refund.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Obtain written supplier/TBO/EPS confirmation where possible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify refund amount, line item, commission impact, TSP/goodwill treatment, and booking balance.</p></li>\n<li><p>Correct any underpaid/imbalanced booking condition before opening the refund process.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Adjust/cancel the applicable line item to reflect the approved amount.</p></li>\n<li><p>For a full line-item refund, cancel/zero the applicable line when appropriate.</p></li>\n<li><p>For a partial refund, use the correct line-item adjustment method.</p></li>\n<li><p>Ensure the booking balance reflects the amount to be returned.</p></li>\n<li><p>Open/submit the required refund workflow/queue.</p></li>\n<li><p>Advise the advisor of the refund amount and 7–10 business-day processing timeframe.</p></li>\n<li><p>Advise the advisor if commission is being recalled or changed.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>TBO confirms refund in writing</td>\n<td>Training allows CS to proceed from written confirmation; CS may not have a direct tool to see when TBO funds physically arrive.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>EPS/Affiliate refund</td>\n<td>Use available affiliate tooling (training referenced Voyager) when applicable to verify supplier-side refund.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Urgent refund</td>\n<td>Email sjctafinance@classicvacations.com with the required details; Finance guide says urgent requests should also copy Tara Cardona and Lina Hernandez.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Booking is not balanced</td>\n<td>Fix/investigate before refund submission; Finance may kick it back and delay the refund.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Supplier approval, amount, calculation, booking adjustment, commission treatment, refund workflow, advisor advisement.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Refund amount or supplier position is unclear; booking cannot be balanced; expedited refund requires leadership/Finance assistance.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Booking shows the correct financial state, refund workflow is submitted, advisor is advised, and required follow-up is owned.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not send a refund to Finance until the booking is financially correct and the supplier approval/refund basis is documented. Use when: Supplier waives penalty, authorizes full/partial refund, TBO/EPS confirms refund, or Classic approves an adjustment requiring a customer refund. Before you start Obtain written supplier/TBO/EPS confirmation where possible. Verify refund amount, line item, commission impact, TSP/goodwill treatment, and booking balance. Correct any underpaid/imbalanced booking condition before opening the refund process. Steps Adjust/cancel the applicable line item to reflect the approved amount. For a full line-item refund, cancel/zero the applicable line when appropriate. For a partial refund, use the correct line-item adjustment method. Ensure the booking balance reflects the amount to be returned. Open/submit the required refund workflow/queue. Advise the advisor of the refund amount and 7–10 business-day processing timeframe. Advise the advisor if commission is being recalled or changed. If / Then If Then TBO confirms refund in writing Training allows CS to proceed from written confirmation; CS may not have a direct tool to see when TBO funds physically arrive. EPS/Affiliate refund Use available affiliate tooling (training referenced Voyager) when applicable to verify supplier-side refund. Urgent refund Email sjctafinance@classicvacations.com with the required details; Finance guide says urgent requests should also copy Tara Cardona and Lina Hernandez. Booking is not balanced Fix/investigate before refund submission; Finance may kick it back and delay the refund. Document Supplier approval, amount, calculation, booking adjustment, commission treatment, refund workflow, advisor advisement. ESCALATE WHEN Refund amount or supplier position is unclear; booking cannot be balanced; expedited refund requires leadership/Finance assistance. COMPLETE WHEN Booking shows the correct financial state, refund workflow is submitted, advisor is advised, and required follow-up is owned."},{"id":"12-2","heading":"12.2 Partial Hotel Night Refund","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> For in-travel hotel-night adjustments, use the average nightly rate of that hotel line item rather than trying to reconstruct the supplier’s varying nightly charge.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Hotel authorizes one or more unused nights/partial stay refund while traveler is in travel.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm total hotel line-item amount and number of nights represented by the line.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm exactly how many nights the supplier authorized.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Check the rate structure before calculating the refund</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Review the hotel rate for free-night promotions such as 4th Night Free, 5th Night Free, or similar offers.</p></li>\n<li><p>When a free-night promotion applies, calculate the average using the number of nights actually charged rather than automatically dividing by the total number of nights stayed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review any minimum-length-of-stay requirement before shortening the stay or applying a TSP-related adjustment. Reducing the stay below the required minimum may create additional financial consequences that must be understood before the adjustment is completed.</p></li>\n<li><p>When applicable, also verify whether seasonal or date-specific rate conditions affect the calculation.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>After confirming the rate structure, calculate the applicable average nightly rate using the number of paid nights represented by the hotel line item.</p></li>\n<li><p>Multiply average nightly rate by number of nights approved for refund.</p></li>\n<li><p>Adjust the hotel line item by that amount.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review and adjust commission according to the applicable rules.</p></li>\n<li><p>Submit refund workflow and advise advisor.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Calculation and supplier authorization.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> The booking structure makes the average-night calculation unclear (multiple rooms/rates/occupancies) or supplier approval is expressed in a different fixed amount.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Line item, commission, and refund queue all match the approved refund.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE For in-travel hotel-night adjustments, use the average nightly rate of that hotel line item rather than trying to reconstruct the supplier’s varying nightly charge. Use when: Hotel authorizes one or more unused nights/partial stay refund while traveler is in travel. Before you start Confirm total hotel line-item amount and number of nights represented by the line. Confirm exactly how many nights the supplier authorized. Check the rate structure before calculating the refund Review the hotel rate for free-night promotions such as 4th Night Free, 5th Night Free, or similar offers. When a free-night promotion applies, calculate the average using the number of nights actually charged rather than automatically dividing by the total number of nights stayed. Review any minimum-length-of-stay requirement before shortening the stay or applying a TSP-related adjustment. Reducing the stay below the required minimum may create additional financial consequences that must be understood before the adjustment is completed. When applicable, also verify whether seasonal or date-specific rate conditions affect the calculation. Steps After confirming the rate structure, calculate the applicable average nightly rate using the number of paid nights represented by the hotel line item. Multiply average nightly rate by number of nights approved for refund. Adjust the hotel line item by that amount. Review and adjust commission according to the applicable rules. Submit refund workflow and advise advisor. Document Calculation and supplier authorization. ESCALATE WHEN The booking structure makes the average-night calculation unclear (multiple rooms/rates/occupancies) or supplier approval is expressed in a different fixed amount. COMPLETE WHEN Line item, commission, and refund queue all match the approved refund."},{"id":"12-3","heading":"12.3 Before Quoting a Cancellation Penalty","html":"<p><strong>Check before quoting a cancellation penalty</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>What component is being canceled?</p></li>\n<li><p>Has any portion already been consumed?</p></li>\n<li><p>What do the booking terms show?</p></li>\n<li><p>Is the supplier penalty confirmed, or does the supplier need to be contacted?</p></li>\n<li><p>Is TSP present, and is the issue a waiver question or an insurance question?</p></li>\n<li><p>Does the cancellation affect other components?</p></li>\n<li><p>Will the refund change commission?</p></li>\n<li><p>Is this FIT, Group, TBO, EPS, CAD, or another source with different rules?</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not quote a waiver, refund, or reduced penalty as final until the controlling source has confirmed it.</div>","text":"Check before quoting a cancellation penalty What component is being canceled? Has any portion already been consumed? What do the booking terms show? Is the supplier penalty confirmed, or does the supplier need to be contacted? Is TSP present, and is the issue a waiver question or an insurance question? Does the cancellation affect other components? Will the refund change commission? Is this FIT, Group, TBO, EPS, CAD, or another source with different rules? POLICY / RULE Do not quote a waiver, refund, or reduced penalty as final until the controlling source has confirmed it."}]},{"id":"13","number":"13","title":"Financial Adjustments","fullTitle":"13. Financial Adjustments","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Choose the adjustment level based on what changed financially. A line-item adjustment changes a specific component. Booking-level adjustments are used for whole-booking commission adjustments and TA/CS goodwill or error-related situations described by management.</div><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Adjustment</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Use it for</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Examples</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Line-Item Adjustment</td>\n<td>Any financial adjustment to a specific component.</td>\n<td>Vendor-approved refund/increase; hotel refund due to TSP; partial service refund.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Booking-Level Adjustment</td>\n<td>Whole-booking commission or CS/TA goodwill/error-related financial handling.</td>\n<td>Commission adjustment as a whole; TA goodwill/error on CS side; paying for a service from commission; TSP in-travel commission protection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goodwill-specific system option</td>\n<td>Management did not separately define the exact Plex label/selection in the clarification response.</td>\n<td>Follow the current Plex adjustment option used by CS leadership; see Appendix C maintenance item.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"RULE Choose the adjustment level based on what changed financially. A line-item adjustment changes a specific component. Booking-level adjustments are used for whole-booking commission adjustments and TA/CS goodwill or error-related situations described by management. Adjustment Use it for Examples Line-Item Adjustment Any financial adjustment to a specific component. Vendor-approved refund/increase; hotel refund due to TSP; partial service refund. Booking-Level Adjustment Whole-booking commission or CS/TA goodwill/error-related financial handling. Commission adjustment as a whole; TA goodwill/error on CS side; paying for a service from commission; TSP in-travel commission protection. Goodwill-specific system option Management did not separately define the exact Plex label/selection in the clarification response. Follow the current Plex adjustment option used by CS leadership; see Appendix C maintenance item.","blocks":[{"id":"13-1","heading":"13.1 Line-Item Adjustment","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Adjust the component to the exact approved financial value; do not use a booking-level adjustment to hide or offset a component-level refund.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Supplier authorizes a partial refund/increase or TSP-related hotel refund.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm approval amount and affected component.</p></li>\n<li><p>Calculate the correct new line-item value.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Open the line item adjustment.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter the approved adjustment so the component reflects the new financial value.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review resulting commission and booking balance.</p></li>\n<li><p>Add refund workflow if money is due back to customer.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Approval source, math, line adjusted, commission impact.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> The adjustment cannot be tied cleanly to one line item or the financial result is not understood.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Component, commission, and booking balance all match the approved outcome. Review Mod History after saving the adjustment and confirm the final sell, cost, commission, and booking balance match the intended result.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Adjust the component to the exact approved financial value; do not use a booking-level adjustment to hide or offset a component-level refund. Use when: Supplier authorizes a partial refund/increase or TSP-related hotel refund. Before you start Confirm approval amount and affected component. Calculate the correct new line-item value. Steps Open the line item adjustment. Enter the approved adjustment so the component reflects the new financial value. Review resulting commission and booking balance. Add refund workflow if money is due back to customer. Document Approval source, math, line adjusted, commission impact. ESCALATE WHEN The adjustment cannot be tied cleanly to one line item or the financial result is not understood. COMPLETE WHEN Component, commission, and booking balance all match the approved outcome. Review Mod History after saving the adjustment and confirm the final sell, cost, commission, and booking balance match the intended result."},{"id":"13-2","heading":"13.2 Supplier-Funded vs. Classic/TSP-Funded Adjustments","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Determine who is absorbing the financial loss before changing supplier cost.</div>\n<p><strong>Supplier-funded refund</strong></p>\n<p>If the vendor approves a refund or waives all or part of the amount owed to Classic:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Adjust the customer-facing sell amount to the approved value.</p></li>\n<li><p>Adjust commission as required unless commission is being protected.</p></li>\n<li><p>Adjust supplier cost to reflect the amount the vendor has agreed to waive/refund.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Classic/TSP-funded refund</strong></p>\n<p>If the vendor is not refunding Classic and Classic/TSP is providing the customer relief:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Adjust the customer-facing amount according to the approved resolution.</p></li>\n<li><p>Handle commission according to the applicable commission-protection rules.</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not reduce supplier cost when Classic is still responsible for paying the vendor.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">WHY THIS MATTERS</span> A customer refund does not automatically mean Classic's supplier obligation changed. Supplier cost should reflect what Classic actually owes the vendor.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Determine who is absorbing the financial loss before changing supplier cost. Supplier-funded refund If the vendor approves a refund or waives all or part of the amount owed to Classic: Adjust the customer-facing sell amount to the approved value. Adjust commission as required unless commission is being protected. Adjust supplier cost to reflect the amount the vendor has agreed to waive/refund. Classic/TSP-funded refund If the vendor is not refunding Classic and Classic/TSP is providing the customer relief: Adjust the customer-facing amount according to the approved resolution. Handle commission according to the applicable commission-protection rules. Do not reduce supplier cost when Classic is still responsible for paying the vendor. WHY THIS MATTERS A customer refund does not automatically mean Classic's supplier obligation changed. Supplier cost should reflect what Classic actually owes the vendor."},{"id":"13-3","heading":"13.3 Financial Action Quick Guide","html":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Situation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Primary Action</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Vendor approves full or partial refund</td><td>Line-item adjustment + refund workflow + commission review</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Vendor approves refund and also protects advisor commission</td><td>Line-item adjustment + refund; leave protected commission intact</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Vendor does not refund Classic, but TSP/Classic provides traveler relief</td><td>Customer adjustment/refund; do not reduce supplier cost</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Qualifying TSP in-travel change reduces advisor commission</td><td>Apply eligible commission protection, up to remaining $100 per booking</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Classic service-recovery compensation</td><td>Goodwill / booking-level adjustment within authority</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Future-value recovery is more appropriate than cash</td><td>FTC within authority</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Refund or reduction lowers commission and no protection applies</td><td>Adjust/recall commission and advise TA</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Advisor asks to reduce the client's refund to preserve commission</td><td>Do not reduce the client's approved refund for this purpose</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Group financial change</td><td>Follow Group-specific financial procedures in Section 19</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","text":"Situation Primary Action Vendor approves full or partial refund Line-item adjustment + refund workflow + commission review Vendor approves refund and also protects advisor commission Line-item adjustment + refund; leave protected commission intact Vendor does not refund Classic, but TSP/Classic provides traveler relief Customer adjustment/refund; do not reduce supplier cost Qualifying TSP in-travel change reduces advisor commission Apply eligible commission protection, up to remaining $100 per booking Classic service-recovery compensation Goodwill / booking-level adjustment within authority Future-value recovery is more appropriate than cash FTC within authority Refund or reduction lowers commission and no protection applies Adjust/recall commission and advise TA Advisor asks to reduce the client's refund to preserve commission Do not reduce the client's approved refund for this purpose Group financial change Follow Group-specific financial procedures in Section 19"}]}]},{"id":"commission-vcc","label":"Commission, Fees & VCC/Payment Support","items":[{"id":"14","number":"14","title":"Commission, Agency Fees & Commission Protection","fullTitle":"14. Commission, Agency Fees & Commission Protection","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">KEEP THESE SEPARATE</span> $100 Goodwill Authority and $100 In-Travel Commission Protection are different policies. Goodwill compensates a service issue. Commission protection protects advisor commission and requires TSP plus a qualifying in-travel change.</div>","introText":"KEEP THESE SEPARATE $100 Goodwill Authority and $100 In-Travel Commission Protection are different policies. Goodwill compensates a service issue. Commission protection protects advisor commission and requires TSP plus a qualifying in-travel change.","blocks":[{"id":"14-1","heading":"14.1 In-Travel Commission Protection","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Maximum: up to $100 total per booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Applies to in-travel changes only.</p></li>\n<li><p>TSP must be on the booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is per booking, not per line item.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review notes/history to ensure prior in-travel commission protection has not already used part of the $100.</p></li>\n<li><p>For a full cancellation with TSP, direct the advisor to the formal Commission Protection Claim process rather than treating it as the $100 in-travel change courtesy.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Maximum: up to $100 total per booking. Applies to in-travel changes only. TSP must be on the booking. It is per booking, not per line item. Review notes/history to ensure prior in-travel commission protection has not already used part of the $100. For a full cancellation with TSP, direct the advisor to the formal Commission Protection Claim process rather than treating it as the $100 in-travel change courtesy."},{"id":"14-2","heading":"14.2 Commission Recall / Adjustment","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Whenever a refund or price reduction changes commission, calculate and document the commission impact and advise the travel advisor when commission will be recalled.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Refund, early departure, line-item reduction, cancellation, or other change that reduces commission.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm whether the supplier has agreed to protect the advisor’s commission. Supplier-protected commission is separate from Classic’s TSP commission-protection benefit and separate from CS goodwill.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review original commission and the adjusted component value.</p></li>\n<li><p>Check whether TSP-based in-travel commission protection applies.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Calculate the correct commission after the financial change.</p></li>\n<li><p>Apply/route the commission adjustment.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the supplier has agreed to protect the commission, preserve the approved commission amount when completing the financial adjustment and document the supplier approval.</p></li>\n<li><p>If supplier protection does not apply, check whether the confirmed TSP in-travel commission-protection rule applies.</p></li>\n<li><p>If neither protection applies, adjust/recall commission as required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Advise the travel advisor of any recall/reduction.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Original/adjusted commission, protection used/remaining, advisor advisement.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">CLIENT REFUND RULE</span> Do not reduce an approved client refund simply to preserve the advisor’s commission. The client’s refund entitlement and the advisor’s commission treatment must be handled separately.</div><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Commission treatment is ambiguous, a whole-booking adjustment is required, or request exceeds the confirmed $100 protection.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Booking shows correct commission and advisor has been advised.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Whenever a refund or price reduction changes commission, calculate and document the commission impact and advise the travel advisor when commission will be recalled. Use when: Refund, early departure, line-item reduction, cancellation, or other change that reduces commission. Before you start Confirm whether the supplier has agreed to protect the advisor’s commission. Supplier-protected commission is separate from Classic’s TSP commission-protection benefit and separate from CS goodwill. Review original commission and the adjusted component value. Check whether TSP-based in-travel commission protection applies. Steps Calculate the correct commission after the financial change. Apply/route the commission adjustment. If the supplier has agreed to protect the commission, preserve the approved commission amount when completing the financial adjustment and document the supplier approval. If supplier protection does not apply, check whether the confirmed TSP in-travel commission-protection rule applies. If neither protection applies, adjust/recall commission as required. Advise the travel advisor of any recall/reduction. Document Original/adjusted commission, protection used/remaining, advisor advisement. CLIENT REFUND RULE Do not reduce an approved client refund simply to preserve the advisor’s commission. The client’s refund entitlement and the advisor’s commission treatment must be handled separately. ESCALATE WHEN Commission treatment is ambiguous, a whole-booking adjustment is required, or request exceeds the confirmed $100 protection. COMPLETE WHEN Booking shows correct commission and advisor has been advised."},{"id":"14-3","heading":"14.3 Additional Commission From In-Travel Additions","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> When CS takes payment for an in-travel addition that generates commission, remember to request/pay the additional commission.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Stay extension, added service/tour, or other paid in-travel addition.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm added component and payment collected.</p></li>\n<li><p>Calculate additional commission.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Open the commission request/internal workflow.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter booking number and additional commission amount as required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the request.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Added component/payment and commission request.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Commission calculation or payout method is unclear.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Commission request is submitted and documented.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE When CS takes payment for an in-travel addition that generates commission, remember to request/pay the additional commission. Use when: Stay extension, added service/tour, or other paid in-travel addition. Before you start Confirm added component and payment collected. Calculate additional commission. Steps Open the commission request/internal workflow. Enter booking number and additional commission amount as required. Document the request. Document Added component/payment and commission request. ESCALATE WHEN Commission calculation or payout method is unclear. COMPLETE WHEN Commission request is submitted and documented."},{"id":"14-4","heading":"14.4 Planning / Agency Fee In Travel","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not add an agency/planning fee during travel unless CS is also making a booking modification that requires payment.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Advisor asks CS to add an agency fee while the client is already traveling.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm there is an actual modification with an amount due.</p></li>\n<li><p>Training stated planning fee should not exceed $10,000; use current system/policy if the limit changes.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Make the booking modification.</p></li>\n<li><p>Add the agency/planning fee.</p></li>\n<li><p>Take payment for both the modification and the fee.</p></li>\n<li><p>Open the required agency-fee payout/internal queue.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>No modification / no payment due</td>\n<td>Do not add the fee by itself.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Modification, fee amount, payment, payout workflow.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Advisor disputes the restriction or requests an exception.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Payment and agency-fee payout are both complete/routed.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not add an agency/planning fee during travel unless CS is also making a booking modification that requires payment. Use when: Advisor asks CS to add an agency fee while the client is already traveling. Before you start Confirm there is an actual modification with an amount due. Training stated planning fee should not exceed $10,000; use current system/policy if the limit changes. Steps Make the booking modification. Add the agency/planning fee. Take payment for both the modification and the fee. Open the required agency-fee payout/internal queue. If / Then If Then No modification / no payment due Do not add the fee by itself. Document Modification, fee amount, payment, payout workflow. ESCALATE WHEN Advisor disputes the restriction or requests an exception. COMPLETE WHEN Payment and agency-fee payout are both complete/routed."}]},{"id":"15","number":"15","title":"VCC / Hotel Payment Support","fullTitle":"15. VCC / Hotel Payment Support","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">FINANCE OWNERSHIP</span> Finance Operations supports vendor payment, TA commissions, refunds, chargebacks, VCC support/reconciliation, CyberSource questions, vendor setup/updates. Accounting handles back-end reconciliation/reporting/audits/financial statements and record keeping.</div>","introText":"FINANCE OWNERSHIP Finance Operations supports vendor payment, TA commissions, refunds, chargebacks, VCC support/reconciliation, CyberSource questions, vendor setup/updates. Accounting handles back-end reconciliation/reporting/audits/financial statements and record keeping.","blocks":[{"id":"15-1","heading":"15.1 VCC Issues Covered by Finance","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>VCC link expired.</p></li>\n<li><p>VCC was never received.</p></li>\n<li><p>Vendor cannot locate the system-generated VCC link.</p></li>\n<li><p>VCC is needed for a CAD booking to secure the reservation.</p></li>\n<li><p>VCC was received but declined due to insufficient funds.</p></li>\n<li><p>VCC declined because activation is delayed.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"VCC link expired. VCC was never received. Vendor cannot locate the system-generated VCC link. VCC is needed for a CAD booking to secure the reservation. VCC was received but declined due to insufficient funds. VCC declined because activation is delayed."},{"id":"15-2","heading":"15.2 Standard VCC Request","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> The vendor should submit the Finance VCC Smartsheet request. The Finance guide also allows CS to open it for the vendor when needed, provided a vendor contact is included.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Vendor contacts CS with a VCC problem.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm the property is VCC-paid rather than invoice-paid.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify the exact problem and booking/CAD details.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Provide the vendor the VCC request form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b</p></li>\n<li><p>Ask the vendor to submit the ticket. If CS submits on the vendor’s behalf, include a valid vendor contact for Finance follow-up.</p></li>\n<li><p>During Finance hours, use the Finance queue if immediate assistance is needed: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM, (408) 794-3200.</p></li>\n<li><p>For urgent CAD VCC creation, use the separate Urgent VCC form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Booking, property, exact VCC issue, ticket/form submission, vendor contact.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Traveler is at check-in/checkout, property threatens to charge traveler, or issue occurs after Finance hours.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Finance ticket is submitted and the vendor/traveler has a clear immediate plan.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE The vendor should submit the Finance VCC Smartsheet request. The Finance guide also allows CS to open it for the vendor when needed, provided a vendor contact is included. Use when: Vendor contacts CS with a VCC problem. Before you start Confirm the property is VCC-paid rather than invoice-paid. Identify the exact problem and booking/CAD details. Steps Provide the vendor the VCC request form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b Ask the vendor to submit the ticket. If CS submits on the vendor’s behalf, include a valid vendor contact for Finance follow-up. During Finance hours, use the Finance queue if immediate assistance is needed: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM, (408) 794-3200. For urgent CAD VCC creation, use the separate Urgent VCC form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8 Document Booking, property, exact VCC issue, ticket/form submission, vendor contact. ESCALATE WHEN Traveler is at check-in/checkout, property threatens to charge traveler, or issue occurs after Finance hours. COMPLETE WHEN Finance ticket is submitted and the vendor/traveler has a clear immediate plan."},{"id":"15-3","heading":"15.3 Hotel Charged Traveler Directly","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Treat an erroneous direct hotel charge on a prepaid booking as urgent. Contact the property immediately for reversal and escalate payment support so the traveler is not left without access to funds while still traveling.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Hotel charges traveler for a prepaid stay or places a large improper charge/hold.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Verify booking was prepaid and identify amount charged/held.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm whether charge is pending/posted and whether property acknowledges error.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact the property and request immediate reversal/release.</p></li>\n<li><p>Escalate to Finance/leadership as required; do not simply tell the traveler to wait several business days if the charge creates active travel hardship.</p></li>\n<li><p>If after hours/weekend, contact CS leadership; leadership uses the Teams channel “VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support.”</p></li>\n<li><p>Document all amounts, contacts, reversal reference, and expected timing.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Charge amount, property contact, reversal/hold release, leadership/Finance escalation, traveler impact.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Property will not reverse, traveler cannot continue trip because funds are tied up, or Finance is unavailable during an active in-travel emergency.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> The erroneous charge is reversed/released or an approved interim solution is in place and actively owned.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Treat an erroneous direct hotel charge on a prepaid booking as urgent. Contact the property immediately for reversal and escalate payment support so the traveler is not left without access to funds while still traveling. Use when: Hotel charges traveler for a prepaid stay or places a large improper charge/hold. Before you start Verify booking was prepaid and identify amount charged/held. Confirm whether charge is pending/posted and whether property acknowledges error. Steps Contact the property and request immediate reversal/release. Escalate to Finance/leadership as required; do not simply tell the traveler to wait several business days if the charge creates active travel hardship. If after hours/weekend, contact CS leadership; leadership uses the Teams channel “VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support.” Document all amounts, contacts, reversal reference, and expected timing. Document Charge amount, property contact, reversal/hold release, leadership/Finance escalation, traveler impact. ESCALATE WHEN Property will not reverse, traveler cannot continue trip because funds are tied up, or Finance is unavailable during an active in-travel emergency. COMPLETE WHEN The erroneous charge is reversed/released or an approved interim solution is in place and actively owned."}]}]},{"id":"goodwill-protection","label":"Goodwill, Service Recovery & Trip Protection","items":[{"id":"16","number":"16","title":"Goodwill & Service Recovery","fullTitle":"16. Goodwill & Service Recovery","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">AGENT AUTHORITY</span> CS agents may approve up to $100 goodwill per booking, provided the adjustment does not reduce Classic’s net margin below 5%. If the proposed goodwill would bring the booking below the 5% net-margin threshold, leadership approval is required regardless of the dollar amount. Future Travel Credit (FTC): up to $250 per booking at the CS agent’s discretion for FIT or Groups. Anything above $250 requires leadership approval.</div>","introText":"AGENT AUTHORITY CS agents may approve up to $100 goodwill per booking, provided the adjustment does not reduce Classic’s net margin below 5%. If the proposed goodwill would bring the booking below the 5% net-margin threshold, leadership approval is required regardless of the dollar amount. Future Travel Credit (FTC): up to $250 per booking at the CS agent’s discretion for FIT or Groups. Anything above $250 requires leadership approval.","blocks":[{"id":"16-1","heading":"16.1 Service Recovery Order","html":"<ol>\n<li><p>Fix the service problem while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Seek supplier-provided recovery first when the supplier caused the failure.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use agent goodwill only when appropriate after the operational resolution is understood.</p></li>\n<li><p>Consider FTC when future-value recovery is more appropriate than a cash refund.</p></li>\n<li><p>Escalate when the recommended resolution exceeds authority or the business/relationship risk warrants management judgment.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"Fix the service problem while the traveler is still in destination whenever possible. Seek supplier-provided recovery first when the supplier caused the failure. Use agent goodwill only when appropriate after the operational resolution is understood. Consider FTC when future-value recovery is more appropriate than a cash refund. Escalate when the recommended resolution exceeds authority or the business/relationship risk warrants management judgment."},{"id":"16-2","heading":"16.2 Agent Goodwill","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Goodwill is a service-recovery tool, not an automatic response to dissatisfaction. Maximum frontline authority is $100 per booking.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Classic service failure, exceptional service-recovery need, or approved situation where a small monetary resolution is appropriate.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Review the booking’s current net margin.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the proposed goodwill would reduce net margin below 5%, stop and obtain leadership approval.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review prior goodwill/adjustments on the booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Separate supplier refund owed from Classic-funded goodwill.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Determine the smallest reasonable resolution that addresses the impact.</p></li>\n<li><p>Apply the approved goodwill using the current booking-level adjustment process.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the reason and total goodwill used on the booking.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Request exceeds $100 per booking</td>\n<td>Do not split the amount. Escalate for approval.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Issue is only an unguaranteed request not met</td>\n<td>Attempt operational resolution first; goodwill is not automatic.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Reason, amount, prior goodwill reviewed, outcome.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Any amount beyond $100 or high-profile/relationship-sensitive case needing leadership decision. The proposed adjustment would reduce Classic’s net margin below 5%, even when the goodwill amount is $100 or less.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Financial adjustment is correctly posted and the caller understands the resolution.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Goodwill is a service-recovery tool, not an automatic response to dissatisfaction. Maximum frontline authority is $100 per booking. Use when: Classic service failure, exceptional service-recovery need, or approved situation where a small monetary resolution is appropriate. Before you start Review the booking’s current net margin. If the proposed goodwill would reduce net margin below 5%, stop and obtain leadership approval. Review prior goodwill/adjustments on the booking. Separate supplier refund owed from Classic-funded goodwill. Steps Determine the smallest reasonable resolution that addresses the impact. Apply the approved goodwill using the current booking-level adjustment process. Document the reason and total goodwill used on the booking. If / Then If Then Request exceeds $100 per booking Do not split the amount. Escalate for approval. Issue is only an unguaranteed request not met Attempt operational resolution first; goodwill is not automatic. Document Reason, amount, prior goodwill reviewed, outcome. ESCALATE WHEN Any amount beyond $100 or high-profile/relationship-sensitive case needing leadership decision. The proposed adjustment would reduce Classic’s net margin below 5%, even when the goodwill amount is $100 or less. COMPLETE WHEN Financial adjustment is correctly posted and the caller understands the resolution."},{"id":"16-3","heading":"16.3 Future Travel Credit (FTC)","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> CS agents may issue up to $250 FTC per booking at their discretion for FIT or Groups; above $250 requires leadership approval.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Service recovery is appropriate but immediate cash refund is not required or is not the best retention solution.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Review prior FTC/goodwill and the reason for service recovery.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Determine appropriate FTC amount up to $250.</p></li>\n<li><p>Apply/create FTC using current CS process.</p></li>\n<li><p>Explain validity/redemption terms shown by the current system/process; do not invent terms not displayed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document amount and reason.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Amount, reason, booking, any leadership approval.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> FTC above $250 or unusual contractual/group circumstance.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> FTC is created, communicated, and documented.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE CS agents may issue up to $250 FTC per booking at their discretion for FIT or Groups; above $250 requires leadership approval. Use when: Service recovery is appropriate but immediate cash refund is not required or is not the best retention solution. Before you start Review prior FTC/goodwill and the reason for service recovery. Steps Determine appropriate FTC amount up to $250. Apply/create FTC using current CS process. Explain validity/redemption terms shown by the current system/process; do not invent terms not displayed. Document amount and reason. Document Amount, reason, booking, any leadership approval. ESCALATE WHEN FTC above $250 or unusual contractual/group circumstance. COMPLETE WHEN FTC is created, communicated, and documented."}]},{"id":"17","number":"17","title":"Trip Protection in Customer Service","fullTitle":"17. Trip Protection in Customer Service","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> CS may explain operational rules visible in the booking and plan documents, but should not promise an insurance claim outcome. The insurance portion is handled through TripMate; CS should refer detailed coverage/claim questions accordingly.</div>","introText":"RULE CS may explain operational rules visible in the booking and plan documents, but should not promise an insurance claim outcome. The insurance portion is handled through TripMate; CS should refer detailed coverage/claim questions accordingly.","blocks":[{"id":"17-1","heading":"17.1 CS TSP Responsibilities","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Always check whether TSP is on the booking when an in-travel cancellation/change or commission impact is involved.</p></li>\n<li><p>Open the plan details and use the actual terms/“not covered” information rather than assuming coverage from the reason for travel disruption.</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not promise that a medical or other claim will be reimbursed merely because TSP exists.</p></li>\n<li><p>For insurance/Part B claim specifics, refer to TripMate. Training emphasized that CS is not acting as a licensed insurance agent.</p></li>\n<li><p>Even when TSP may apply, continue to pursue supplier waivers/refunds when appropriate; reducing supplier penalties benefits the booking and claim exposure.</p></li>\n<li><p>For full cancellation commission protection, use the formal Commission Protection Claim process.</p></li>\n<li><p>Group TSP was trained as more restrictive and primarily insurance/Part B driven; use current Group TSP terms and refer claims to TripMate rather than promising a waiver.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMMISSION RULE</span> TSP + qualifying in-travel change: CS may protect up to $100 commission total per booking. Full cancellation: use the formal commission-protection claim path instead.</div>","text":"Always check whether TSP is on the booking when an in-travel cancellation/change or commission impact is involved. Open the plan details and use the actual terms/“not covered” information rather than assuming coverage from the reason for travel disruption. Do not promise that a medical or other claim will be reimbursed merely because TSP exists. For insurance/Part B claim specifics, refer to TripMate. Training emphasized that CS is not acting as a licensed insurance agent. Even when TSP may apply, continue to pursue supplier waivers/refunds when appropriate; reducing supplier penalties benefits the booking and claim exposure. For full cancellation commission protection, use the formal Commission Protection Claim process. Group TSP was trained as more restrictive and primarily insurance/Part B driven; use current Group TSP terms and refer claims to TripMate rather than promising a waiver. COMMISSION RULE TSP + qualifying in-travel change: CS may protect up to $100 commission total per booking. Full cancellation: use the formal commission-protection claim path instead."}]}]},{"id":"cad-groups","label":"CAD, Manual Components & Groups","items":[{"id":"18","number":"18","title":"CAD & Manual / In-Travel Components","fullTitle":"18. CAD & Manual / In-Travel Components","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Use CAD/manual processes when the needed component cannot be handled through the normal live booking path. In travel, confirm current dates, vendor availability, price, payment, and VCC requirements before representing the service as confirmed.</div>","introText":"RULE Use CAD/manual processes when the needed component cannot be handled through the normal live booking path. In travel, confirm current dates, vendor availability, price, payment, and VCC requirements before representing the service as confirmed.","blocks":[{"id":"18-1","heading":"18.1 In-Travel CAD / Extension","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not treat an in-travel extension as a brand-new quote if the operational task is extending an existing stay/service; use the existing booking context and obtain the appropriate current rate/confirmation.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> CS needs to add/extend a hotel or manually secure another component during travel.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Review current component and traveler dates.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify supplier/source and whether VCC is required to secure.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Contact supplier/CAD source for availability and price.</p></li>\n<li><p>Build/add the component using the correct dates and customer comments.</p></li>\n<li><p>Take payment as required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Request urgent CAD VCC if required to secure the booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Send/communicate confirmation and update related components.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Vendor confirmation, price, dates, payment, VCC request, downstream updates.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Supplier cannot confirm, traveler is without lodging/service, or financial exposure exceeds authority.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> New/extended component is confirmed, paid/secured, and communicated.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not treat an in-travel extension as a brand-new quote if the operational task is extending an existing stay/service; use the existing booking context and obtain the appropriate current rate/confirmation. Use when: CS needs to add/extend a hotel or manually secure another component during travel. Before you start Review current component and traveler dates. Identify supplier/source and whether VCC is required to secure. Steps Contact supplier/CAD source for availability and price. Build/add the component using the correct dates and customer comments. Take payment as required. Request urgent CAD VCC if required to secure the booking. Send/communicate confirmation and update related components. Document Vendor confirmation, price, dates, payment, VCC request, downstream updates. ESCALATE WHEN Supplier cannot confirm, traveler is without lodging/service, or financial exposure exceeds authority. COMPLETE WHEN New/extended component is confirmed, paid/secured, and communicated."}]},{"id":"19","number":"19","title":"Groups","fullTitle":"19. Groups","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">GROUP RULE</span> Group contracts and rooming-list rules control. Do not apply normal FIT assumptions to Group penalties, no-shows, changes, or TSP.</div>","introText":"GROUP RULE Group contracts and rooming-list rules control. Do not apply normal FIT assumptions to Group penalties, no-shows, changes, or TSP.","blocks":[{"id":"19-1","heading":"19.1 Group-Specific Principles","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Groups may enter penalty much earlier than FIT bookings.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hotel rights and change/cancellation consequences are governed by the group contract.</p></li>\n<li><p>A first-night no-show caused by an airline disruption may still remain penalized under the hotel/group contract; seek waiver but do not promise one.</p></li>\n<li><p>The Groups team is responsible for loading core group information; if required data is missing/incorrect, involve Groups management.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use Groups Manager/rooming list to review group details and requests.</p></li>\n<li><p>Group TSP is different/more restrictive; use current Group TSP terms and TripMate for insurance claim handling.</p></li>\n<li><p>CS may issue FTC up to $250 per booking for Group service recovery; above $250 requires leadership approval.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Groups may enter penalty much earlier than FIT bookings. Hotel rights and change/cancellation consequences are governed by the group contract. A first-night no-show caused by an airline disruption may still remain penalized under the hotel/group contract; seek waiver but do not promise one. The Groups team is responsible for loading core group information; if required data is missing/incorrect, involve Groups management. Use Groups Manager/rooming list to review group details and requests. Group TSP is different/more restrictive; use current Group TSP terms and TripMate for insurance claim handling. CS may issue FTC up to $250 per booking for Group service recovery; above $250 requires leadership approval."},{"id":"19-2","heading":"19.2 Work a Group In-Travel Issue","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Review the group contract/rooming data before changing or promising anything.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Group traveler has hotel, transfer, rooming, cancellation, or service problem.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Identify group and traveler/room.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review Groups Manager/rooming list and applicable contract/penalty information.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Resolve immediate traveler need.</p></li>\n<li><p>Contact hotel/vendor and seek waiver/correction as appropriate.</p></li>\n<li><p>Coordinate with Groups leadership if contract interpretation, rooming-list correction, or group-level action is required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Apply CS goodwill/FTC only within confirmed authority and with awareness of group contract implications.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Group/room, contract/penalty facts, supplier response, Groups contact, resolution.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Contract interpretation is required, group-wide impact exists, or requested financial exception exceeds CS authority.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Traveler issue is resolved and group records/owners are aligned.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Review the group contract/rooming data before changing or promising anything. Use when: Group traveler has hotel, transfer, rooming, cancellation, or service problem. Before you start Identify group and traveler/room. Review Groups Manager/rooming list and applicable contract/penalty information. Steps Resolve immediate traveler need. Contact hotel/vendor and seek waiver/correction as appropriate. Coordinate with Groups leadership if contract interpretation, rooming-list correction, or group-level action is required. Apply CS goodwill/FTC only within confirmed authority and with awareness of group contract implications. Document Group/room, contract/penalty facts, supplier response, Groups contact, resolution. ESCALATE WHEN Contract interpretation is required, group-wide impact exists, or requested financial exception exceeds CS authority. COMPLETE WHEN Traveler issue is resolved and group records/owners are aligned."},{"id":"19-3","heading":"19.3 Groups Manager vs. Plex","html":"<p>Groups Manager is separate from Plex, and group reservations are structured differently from standard FIT bookings.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>A Plex booking generally represents one reservation.</p></li>\n<li><p>In Groups Manager, one overall Group ID can contain many individual bookings or rooms.</p></li>\n<li><p>A group may contain dozens or more than 100 individual bookings.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">EXAMPLE</span> <strong>63498</strong> = Group ID. <strong>63498-10</strong> = Booking/Room 10 within that group.</div>\n<p><strong>Each booking may have different</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Travelers</p></li>\n<li><p>Arrival and departure dates</p></li>\n<li><p>Room categories</p></li>\n<li><p>Occupancy</p></li>\n<li><p>Components</p></li>\n<li><p>Payment activity</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Always identify the specific booking/room involved before troubleshooting an issue.</div>","text":"Groups Manager is separate from Plex, and group reservations are structured differently from standard FIT bookings. A Plex booking generally represents one reservation. In Groups Manager, one overall Group ID can contain many individual bookings or rooms. A group may contain dozens or more than 100 individual bookings. EXAMPLE 63498 = Group ID. 63498-10 = Booking/Room 10 within that group. Each booking may have different Travelers Arrival and departure dates Room categories Occupancy Components Payment activity POLICY / RULE Always identify the specific booking/room involved before troubleshooting an issue."},{"id":"19-4","heading":"19.4 Finding a Group","html":"<p>When you first enter Groups Manager, there are two primary ways CS will locate a group.</p>\n<p><strong>View Group</strong></p>\n<p>Use View Group when the Group ID is already known.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Enter the Group ID.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select Go To.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>This is the fastest way to access the group.</p>\n<p><strong>Search Groups</strong></p>\n<p>Use Search Groups when the caller does not know the Group ID. For CS, the most common method is Search By Pax Name.</p>\n<p><strong>Search By Pax Name</strong></p>\n<p>Enter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>First Name</p></li>\n<li><p>Last Name</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Most travelers will know their name but may not know their Group ID or individual booking number.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">USE CAUTION WITH COMMON NAMES</span> Groups Manager does not provide the same travel-date search filtering available in Plex. Searching a very common name can return a large number of historical results, and broad searches have historically caused Groups Manager to respond slowly or become unresponsive. If the traveler has a common name, ask whether they can locate their Group ID, booking/room number, or travel documents.</div>","text":"When you first enter Groups Manager, there are two primary ways CS will locate a group. View Group Use View Group when the Group ID is already known. Enter the Group ID. Select Go To. This is the fastest way to access the group. Search Groups Use Search Groups when the caller does not know the Group ID. For CS, the most common method is Search By Pax Name. Search By Pax Name Enter: First Name Last Name Most travelers will know their name but may not know their Group ID or individual booking number. USE CAUTION WITH COMMON NAMES Groups Manager does not provide the same travel-date search filtering available in Plex. Searching a very common name can return a large number of historical results, and broad searches have historically caused Groups Manager to respond slowly or become unresponsive. If the traveler has a common name, ask whether they can locate their Group ID, booking/room number, or travel documents."},{"id":"19-5","heading":"19.5 Search Results & the Main Group Page","html":"<p>After searching, Groups Manager displays matching groups. Results may include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Group ID</p></li>\n<li><p>Booking ID</p></li>\n<li><p>Group Status</p></li>\n<li><p>Sold By</p></li>\n<li><p>Coordinator</p></li>\n<li><p>Group Title</p></li>\n<li><p>Created Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Depart Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Traveler First and Last Name</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Click the applicable group result to open it. The result also provides the Group ID, which can then be used to access the full group directly.</p>\n<p><strong>Main Group Page</strong></p>\n<p>Once a group is opened, the Group page provides the main overview. The group-level navigation includes Group, Contract, History, Pricing, Inventory, Payment, Total, Bookings, Reports, and FinanceVP.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">CS FOCUS</span> CS will primarily use Group, History, Pricing, Payment, Bookings, and Reports.</div>","text":"After searching, Groups Manager displays matching groups. Results may include: Group ID Booking ID Group Status Sold By Coordinator Group Title Created Date Depart Date Traveler First and Last Name Click the applicable group result to open it. The result also provides the Group ID, which can then be used to access the full group directly. Main Group Page Once a group is opened, the Group page provides the main overview. The group-level navigation includes Group, Contract, History, Pricing, Inventory, Payment, Total, Bookings, Reports, and FinanceVP. CS FOCUS CS will primarily use Group, History, Pricing, Payment, Bookings, and Reports."},{"id":"19-6","heading":"19.6 Contact Information, Agent Fields & the Groups Coordinator","html":"<p>The tan Contact Information for this Group section is similar to Agency Information in Plex. It may include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Agency</p></li>\n<li><p>Agency Name</p></li>\n<li><p>Address</p></li>\n<li><p>Territory</p></li>\n<li><p>Booked Consortium</p></li>\n<li><p>Agent</p></li>\n<li><p>Agent Email</p></li>\n<li><p>Agent Login ID</p></li>\n<li><p>GS</p></li>\n<li><p>GC</p></li>\n<li><p>Contract</p></li>\n<li><p>Commission %</p></li>\n<li><p>Phone</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Agent Email vs. Agent Login ID</strong></p>\n<p>These fields serve different purposes.</p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Field</strong></th>\n<th><strong>What it is</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Agent Email</td>\n<td>The advisor's actual communication/contact email. Use this email when CS needs to contact the travel advisor.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Agent Login ID</td>\n<td>Associated with the advisor's login to the group website. Do not assume this is the advisor's communication email.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Groups Coordinator</strong></p>\n<p>GC = Groups Coordinator. The Groups Coordinator is the Classic employee or team responsible for managing the group — generally building the group, advisor communication, group changes, pre-travel servicing, and overall group management. Think of the Groups Coordinator as the Groups equivalent of the booking owner.</p>\n<p>Some high-volume agencies may have a dedicated Classic Groups team rather than one individual coordinator.</p>","text":"The tan Contact Information for this Group section is similar to Agency Information in Plex. It may include: Agency Agency Name Address Territory Booked Consortium Agent Agent Email Agent Login ID GS GC Contract Commission % Phone Agent Email vs. Agent Login ID These fields serve different purposes. Field What it is Agent Email The advisor's actual communication/contact email. Use this email when CS needs to contact the travel advisor. Agent Login ID Associated with the advisor's login to the group website. Do not assume this is the advisor's communication email. Groups Coordinator GC = Groups Coordinator. The Groups Coordinator is the Classic employee or team responsible for managing the group — generally building the group, advisor communication, group changes, pre-travel servicing, and overall group management. Think of the Groups Coordinator as the Groups equivalent of the booking owner. Some high-volume agencies may have a dedicated Classic Groups team rather than one individual coordinator."},{"id":"19-7","heading":"19.7 Group Contract Details & Warnings/Advisories","html":"<p>The Group Contract Details section provides the high-level group information. Fields may include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Group Type</p></li>\n<li><p>Group Status</p></li>\n<li><p>Destination</p></li>\n<li><p>Location</p></li>\n<li><p>Travel From</p></li>\n<li><p>Travel To</p></li>\n<li><p>Booking Lock Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Max Room Cap</p></li>\n<li><p>Hotel Name</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Group Type</strong></p>\n<p>Examples discussed in training include Destination Wedding, Corporate/Incentive, Social Group, and Test. Destination Weddings are one of the most common group types CS may encounter.</p>\n<p><strong>Warnings / Advisories</strong></p>\n<p>The Group page includes a Warnings/Advisories section. Warnings may display information such as hotel name changes, tax increases, construction, property changes, or other operational advisories.</p>\n<p><strong>How to View the Advisory</strong></p>\n<p>Click the teal advisory title. The full WARN/advisory information opens in a pop-up window.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">IMPORTANT</span> Not every group hotel is necessarily a standard Classic Preferred property. The absence of a warning in Groups Manager should not automatically be interpreted as confirmation that no property issue exists.</div>","text":"The Group Contract Details section provides the high-level group information. Fields may include: Group Type Group Status Destination Location Travel From Travel To Booking Lock Date Max Room Cap Hotel Name Group Type Examples discussed in training include Destination Wedding, Corporate/Incentive, Social Group, and Test. Destination Weddings are one of the most common group types CS may encounter. Warnings / Advisories The Group page includes a Warnings/Advisories section. Warnings may display information such as hotel name changes, tax increases, construction, property changes, or other operational advisories. How to View the Advisory Click the teal advisory title. The full WARN/advisory information opens in a pop-up window. IMPORTANT Not every group hotel is necessarily a standard Classic Preferred property. The absence of a warning in Groups Manager should not automatically be interpreted as confirmation that no property issue exists."},{"id":"19-8","heading":"19.8 Bookings (the Room List)","html":"<p>Select Bookings to view all individual room bookings associated with the group. This is one of the primary areas CS will use. The Bookings page may display:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Booking Number</p></li>\n<li><p>Legal Names</p></li>\n<li><p>Guests</p></li>\n<li><p>Room Type</p></li>\n<li><p>Arrival Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Departure Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Nights</p></li>\n<li><p>Hotel</p></li>\n<li><p>Hotel Fee</p></li>\n<li><p>Groups Amount Received</p></li>\n<li><p>Total Sell</p></li>\n<li><p>Amount Due</p></li>\n<li><p>Total Commission</p></li>\n<li><p>Take Payment</p></li>\n<li><p>Request Statement</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Refresh the Booking List</strong></p>\n<p>Groups Manager may not initially load every booking within the group. If the caller provides a room number that is higher than the rooms currently visible, select Refresh and allow the remaining bookings to load, then locate the room again.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not assume the booking does not exist simply because it did not load initially.</div>\n<p><strong>Legal Names and Occupants</strong></p>\n<p>The Legal Names column generally displays the lead two travelers assigned to the room. If more than two travelers are assigned, hover over the names or open the booking to see the additional travelers. Do not rely only on the visible names when confirming occupancy.</p>\n<p><strong>Canceled Bookings</strong></p>\n<p>A booking that is crossed out in the Bookings list generally indicates that the room was canceled. When researching a canceled traveler, review the booking and history before assuming the traveler was never part of the group.</p>","text":"Select Bookings to view all individual room bookings associated with the group. This is one of the primary areas CS will use. The Bookings page may display: Booking Number Legal Names Guests Room Type Arrival Date Departure Date Nights Hotel Hotel Fee Groups Amount Received Total Sell Amount Due Total Commission Take Payment Request Statement Refresh the Booking List Groups Manager may not initially load every booking within the group. If the caller provides a room number that is higher than the rooms currently visible, select Refresh and allow the remaining bookings to load, then locate the room again. POLICY / RULE Do not assume the booking does not exist simply because it did not load initially. Legal Names and Occupants The Legal Names column generally displays the lead two travelers assigned to the room. If more than two travelers are assigned, hover over the names or open the booking to see the additional travelers. Do not rely only on the visible names when confirming occupancy. Canceled Bookings A booking that is crossed out in the Bookings list generally indicates that the room was canceled. When researching a canceled traveler, review the booking and history before assuming the traveler was never part of the group."},{"id":"19-9","heading":"19.9 Opening an Individual Booking","html":"<p>Click or double-click the applicable booking/room line to open the Booking Information page. When an individual booking is opened, the navigation changes to Group, Bookings, Booking Detail, History, Financial Details, Reports, and FinanceVP. To return to the overall group, select Group.</p>\n<p><strong>Booking Information</strong></p>\n<p>The Booking Information page provides room-specific details, which may include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Status</p></li>\n<li><p>Booking #</p></li>\n<li><p>Depart Date</p></li>\n<li><p>Passenger Name</p></li>\n<li><p>Total Sell</p></li>\n<li><p>Commission</p></li>\n<li><p>GM Amount Received</p></li>\n<li><p>Plex Amount Received</p></li>\n<li><p>Amount Due</p></li>\n<li><p>Vendor</p></li>\n<li><p>Product Name</p></li>\n<li><p>Bedding</p></li>\n<li><p>Departure / Arrival</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirmation</p></li>\n<li><p>Days/Nights</p></li>\n<li><p>Adults</p></li>\n<li><p>Children</p></li>\n<li><p>Sell</p></li>\n<li><p>Commission</p></li>\n<li><p>Tax</p></li>\n<li><p>Cost</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The booking detail can be scrolled horizontally to view additional financial fields.</p>\n<p><strong>Product Name and Occupancy</strong></p>\n<p>Room descriptions may include occupancy abbreviations such as SGL, DBL, TPL/TRPL, and QUAD. These indicate the number of occupants, not bedding — for example, DBL means double occupancy, not two beds.</p>\n<p><strong>Bedding</strong></p>\n<p>The Bedding field reflects the requested bedding configuration. It is request only and should not be treated as guaranteed — even if a specific bed type appears in Groups Manager, this does not mean the hotel has confirmed that bedding.</p>\n<p>If a traveler has a bedding issue:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Confirm the booked room category.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm what bedding configurations that room category can accommodate.</p></li>\n<li><p>Contact the hotel if availability or reassignment needs to be verified.</p></li>\n<li><p>Treat the bedding shown in Groups Manager as the request on file, not a guarantee.</p></li>\n</ol>","text":"Click or double-click the applicable booking/room line to open the Booking Information page. When an individual booking is opened, the navigation changes to Group, Bookings, Booking Detail, History, Financial Details, Reports, and FinanceVP. To return to the overall group, select Group. Booking Information The Booking Information page provides room-specific details, which may include: Status Booking # Depart Date Passenger Name Total Sell Commission GM Amount Received Plex Amount Received Amount Due Vendor Product Name Bedding Departure / Arrival Confirmation Days/Nights Adults Children Sell Commission Tax Cost The booking detail can be scrolled horizontally to view additional financial fields. Product Name and Occupancy Room descriptions may include occupancy abbreviations such as SGL, DBL, TPL/TRPL, and QUAD. These indicate the number of occupants, not bedding — for example, DBL means double occupancy, not two beds. Bedding The Bedding field reflects the requested bedding configuration. It is request only and should not be treated as guaranteed — even if a specific bed type appears in Groups Manager, this does not mean the hotel has confirmed that bedding. If a traveler has a bedding issue: Confirm the booked room category. Confirm what bedding configurations that room category can accommodate. Contact the hotel if availability or reassignment needs to be verified. Treat the bedding shown in Groups Manager as the request on file, not a guarantee."},{"id":"19-10","heading":"19.10 Group History & Booking History","html":"<p>The History tab at the group level is similar to Modification History in Plex. It records system activity, changes made to the group, modifications, and manual notes entered by Classic Vacations agents. The most recent entries may require scrolling down through the history.</p>\n<p><strong>Adding Manual Notes</strong></p>\n<p>At the bottom of Group History is the Add a New History Message field.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">BEST PRACTICE</span> Use the Group History when adding CS manual notes. Although individual bookings also have their own History tab, room-level notes can be overlooked by someone reviewing only the overall group. When a note applies to one specific room, include the booking number in the note — e.g. \"Booking #10: TA called regarding bedding concern…\" — so it's clear which booking within the group the note applies to.</div>\n<p><strong>Individual Booking History</strong></p>\n<p>Each room/booking also has its own History tab. Booking History contains activity tied specifically to that room, such as passenger updates, inventory changes, payment activity, and booking-specific modifications. Use this history when researching room-specific activity.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> CS should generally not use booking-level History for manual notes. Use the Group History instead so the note is visible to anyone reviewing the overall group.</div>","text":"The History tab at the group level is similar to Modification History in Plex. It records system activity, changes made to the group, modifications, and manual notes entered by Classic Vacations agents. The most recent entries may require scrolling down through the history. Adding Manual Notes At the bottom of Group History is the Add a New History Message field. BEST PRACTICE Use the Group History when adding CS manual notes. Although individual bookings also have their own History tab, room-level notes can be overlooked by someone reviewing only the overall group. When a note applies to one specific room, include the booking number in the note — e.g. \"Booking #10: TA called regarding bedding concern…\" — so it's clear which booking within the group the note applies to. Individual Booking History Each room/booking also has its own History tab. Booking History contains activity tied specifically to that room, such as passenger updates, inventory changes, payment activity, and booking-specific modifications. Use this history when researching room-specific activity. POLICY / RULE CS should generally not use booking-level History for manual notes. Use the Group History instead so the note is visible to anyone reviewing the overall group."},{"id":"19-11","heading":"19.11 Pricing","html":"<p>The Pricing tab displays room categories and contracted rates for the group. Not every room category shown on the page is necessarily contracted for the group.</p>\n<p><strong>Contracted Room Categories</strong></p>\n<p>The highlighted room categories are the categories contracted for that group. Use those categories when researching pricing for additional nights, stay extensions, occupancy changes, room-category changes, approved adjustments, or refund calculations. Do not assume every room type displayed is available to the group at the contracted rate.</p>\n<p><strong>Expanding Room Pricing</strong></p>\n<p>Click the applicable contracted room category to expand the pricing. The expanded section may show SGL, DBL, TPL, Child Rates, Cost, Sell, Markup, TA Commission, effective dates, and minimum/maximum age.</p>\n<p><strong>Sell vs. Cost</strong></p>\n<p>Sell = the rate communicated to the advisor or traveler. Cost = Classic's net rate.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Always use the Sell rate for advisor/traveler-facing pricing. Do not communicate the Cost/Net rate.</div>\n<p><strong>Example: Extending One Night</strong></p>\n<p>When a traveler wants to extend their stay:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Open the individual booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm the current room category and occupancy.</p></li>\n<li><p>Go to Pricing.</p></li>\n<li><p>Locate the contracted room category.</p></li>\n<li><p>Expand the room category.</p></li>\n<li><p>Locate the applicable occupancy.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use the Sell rate to calculate the additional night.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm the hotel can accommodate the additional night.</p></li>\n<li><p>Collect payment if required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the change in Group History.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">NOTE</span> The pricing shown in Groups Manager does not by itself confirm hotel availability.</div>","text":"The Pricing tab displays room categories and contracted rates for the group. Not every room category shown on the page is necessarily contracted for the group. Contracted Room Categories The highlighted room categories are the categories contracted for that group. Use those categories when researching pricing for additional nights, stay extensions, occupancy changes, room-category changes, approved adjustments, or refund calculations. Do not assume every room type displayed is available to the group at the contracted rate. Expanding Room Pricing Click the applicable contracted room category to expand the pricing. The expanded section may show SGL, DBL, TPL, Child Rates, Cost, Sell, Markup, TA Commission, effective dates, and minimum/maximum age. Sell vs. Cost Sell = the rate communicated to the advisor or traveler. Cost = Classic's net rate. POLICY / RULE Always use the Sell rate for advisor/traveler-facing pricing. Do not communicate the Cost/Net rate. Example: Extending One Night When a traveler wants to extend their stay: Open the individual booking. Confirm the current room category and occupancy. Go to Pricing. Locate the contracted room category. Expand the room category. Locate the applicable occupancy. Use the Sell rate to calculate the additional night. Confirm the hotel can accommodate the additional night. Collect payment if required. Document the change in Group History. NOTE The pricing shown in Groups Manager does not by itself confirm hotel availability."},{"id":"19-12","heading":"19.12 Payments","html":"<p>Groups Manager provides more than one way to process a payment. Where the payment is initiated determines whether it is associated only with the overall group or directly with a specific booking.</p>\n<p><strong>Group-Level Payment</strong></p>\n<p>From the main Group screen:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Select Payment.</p></li>\n<li><p>Under Process Payments, select Process Credit Card.</p></li>\n<li><p>Complete the credit-card and billing information.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter the amount to be paid.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The payment pop-up identifies the Group ID. It does not display an individual Booking ID — this means the payment is being processed at the group level.</p>\n<p><strong>Booking-Specific Payment</strong></p>\n<p>When payment should be applied directly to one room:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Go to Bookings.</p></li>\n<li><p>Locate the correct room.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select PAY under the Take Payment column.</p></li>\n<li><p>Complete the credit-card and billing information.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify the Summary before submitting.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Summary will show both the Group ID and the Booking ID. This confirms the payment is tied to that specific booking.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">BEST PRACTICE</span> For an in-travel change affecting one specific room, use the PAY button for that booking when the payment should be associated directly with the room.</div>\n<p><strong>Payment Routing Quick Rule</strong></p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 34%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Payment Need</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Start From</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Payment Applies To</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Overall group</td>\n<td>Payment → Process Credit Card</td>\n<td>Group ID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Specific room</td>\n<td>Bookings → PAY</td>\n<td>Group ID + Booking ID</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Amount Due</strong></p>\n<p>The Bookings page may show an Amount Due. Do not automatically assume the traveler owes money simply because an amount appears due — group payments may exist at the group level and may still need to be allocated to individual bookings. CS does not manage the overall allocation of group funds. Investigate the payment history before treating an Amount Due as an actual collection issue.</p>\n<p><strong>Reviewing Payments for a Specific Booking</strong></p>\n<p>From the Payment tab, use the Show Payments for booking # dropdown to select the individual room. This allows CS to review the payment activity tied to that booking, which may include Date Received, Deposit Amount Received, Amount Applied to Booking, Unassigned Amount, Credit Card or Check #, Expiration Date, Name on Card, Authorization, Applied to Bookings, and Notes. This is especially important when determining how much can be refunded to a specific card.</p>","text":"Groups Manager provides more than one way to process a payment. Where the payment is initiated determines whether it is associated only with the overall group or directly with a specific booking. Group-Level Payment From the main Group screen: Select Payment. Under Process Payments, select Process Credit Card. Complete the credit-card and billing information. Enter the amount to be paid. The payment pop-up identifies the Group ID. It does not display an individual Booking ID — this means the payment is being processed at the group level. Booking-Specific Payment When payment should be applied directly to one room: Go to Bookings. Locate the correct room. Select PAY under the Take Payment column. Complete the credit-card and billing information. Verify the Summary before submitting. The Summary will show both the Group ID and the Booking ID. This confirms the payment is tied to that specific booking. BEST PRACTICE For an in-travel change affecting one specific room, use the PAY button for that booking when the payment should be associated directly with the room. Payment Routing Quick Rule Payment Need Start From Payment Applies To Overall group Payment → Process Credit Card Group ID Specific room Bookings → PAY Group ID + Booking ID Amount Due The Bookings page may show an Amount Due. Do not automatically assume the traveler owes money simply because an amount appears due — group payments may exist at the group level and may still need to be allocated to individual bookings. CS does not manage the overall allocation of group funds. Investigate the payment history before treating an Amount Due as an actual collection issue. Reviewing Payments for a Specific Booking From the Payment tab, use the Show Payments for booking # dropdown to select the individual room. This allows CS to review the payment activity tied to that booking, which may include Date Received, Deposit Amount Received, Amount Applied to Booking, Unassigned Amount, Credit Card or Check #, Expiration Date, Name on Card, Authorization, Applied to Bookings, and Notes. This is especially important when determining how much can be refunded to a specific card."},{"id":"19-13","heading":"19.13 Refunds","html":"<p>Approved refunds are processed from the Payment tab.</p>\n<p><strong>Process a Refund</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Go to Payment.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use Show Payments for booking # to select the applicable booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify the card/payment to refund.</p></li>\n<li><p>Right-click the credit card number.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select Credit This Card.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter the approved refund amount.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify the amount.</p></li>\n<li><p>Submit the refund.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document the refund in Group History.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Refund Guardrails</strong></p>\n<p>A card can only be refunded up to the amount that was originally charged to that card. If several cards were used, the refund may need to be split among the appropriate cards.</p>\n<p>Before submitting, verify:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Correct Group ID</p></li>\n<li><p>Correct Booking ID</p></li>\n<li><p>Correct card</p></li>\n<li><p>Correct amount</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">CAUTION</span> Groups Manager refunds process directly, so accuracy is critical.</div>","text":"Approved refunds are processed from the Payment tab. Process a Refund Go to Payment. Use Show Payments for booking # to select the applicable booking. Identify the card/payment to refund. Right-click the credit card number. Select Credit This Card. Enter the approved refund amount. Verify the amount. Submit the refund. Document the refund in Group History. Refund Guardrails A card can only be refunded up to the amount that was originally charged to that card. If several cards were used, the refund may need to be split among the appropriate cards. Before submitting, verify: Correct Group ID Correct Booking ID Correct card Correct amount CAUTION Groups Manager refunds process directly, so accuracy is critical."},{"id":"19-14","heading":"19.14 Reports","html":"<p>The Reports tab contains a variety of internal, vendor, and travel-advisor reports. Customer Service will not regularly use most of these. The primary CS functions are Passenger Rooming List, View Docs, and Generate Docs.</p>\n<p><strong>Passenger Rooming List</strong></p>\n<p>The Passenger Rooming List provides a consolidated view of the group's travelers and room assignments.</p>\n<p><strong>Generate a Rooming List</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Go to Reports.</p></li>\n<li><p>Under the Vendor section, select Passenger Rooming List.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select the applicable hotel.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter your email address.</p></li>\n<li><p>Submit the request.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The rooming list will be emailed to you.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> One group may contain more than one hotel. Always select the correct hotel before generating the rooming list.</div>\n<p>The rooming list can help confirm travelers, rooms, room assignments, which travelers are staying together, booking numbers, and hotel assignment.</p>\n<p><strong>Viewing Previously Generated Documents</strong></p>\n<p>On the right side of the Reports page, select View Docs. The Saved Statements window displays previously generated documents, which may include Booking ID, statement/document name, Submitted By, and Submitted Time. Click the applicable item to download the PDF. This is useful when CS needs to review documentation previously sent for a specific booking.</p>\n<p><strong>Resending Documents</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Go to Reports.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select Generate Docs.</p></li>\n<li><p>In Select Bookings for Docs, choose the applicable booking/room.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select OK.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter the recipient's email address.</p></li>\n<li><p>Add an email message if needed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Submit/send the documents.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The email screen also provides options related to how the documents are generated and sent. Always verify that the correct booking is selected before sending documentation.</p>","text":"The Reports tab contains a variety of internal, vendor, and travel-advisor reports. Customer Service will not regularly use most of these. The primary CS functions are Passenger Rooming List, View Docs, and Generate Docs. Passenger Rooming List The Passenger Rooming List provides a consolidated view of the group's travelers and room assignments. Generate a Rooming List Go to Reports. Under the Vendor section, select Passenger Rooming List. Select the applicable hotel. Enter your email address. Submit the request. The rooming list will be emailed to you. POLICY / RULE One group may contain more than one hotel. Always select the correct hotel before generating the rooming list. The rooming list can help confirm travelers, rooms, room assignments, which travelers are staying together, booking numbers, and hotel assignment. Viewing Previously Generated Documents On the right side of the Reports page, select View Docs. The Saved Statements window displays previously generated documents, which may include Booking ID, statement/document name, Submitted By, and Submitted Time. Click the applicable item to download the PDF. This is useful when CS needs to review documentation previously sent for a specific booking. Resending Documents Go to Reports. Select Generate Docs. In Select Bookings for Docs, choose the applicable booking/room. Select OK. Enter the recipient's email address. Add an email message if needed. Submit/send the documents. The email screen also provides options related to how the documents are generated and sent. Always verify that the correct booking is selected before sending documentation."},{"id":"19-15","heading":"19.15 Areas CS Should Use With Caution","html":"<p><strong>Contract</strong></p>\n<p>The Contract area may display contractual information and timelines. Training indicated that CS should not rely solely on this section when making penalty or in-travel policy decisions, as information may not always reflect every subsequent group change. Use it for context only unless otherwise directed.</p>\n<p><strong>Concession Information</strong></p>\n<p>Concessions are negotiated group benefits — examples may include complimentary rooms, welcome events, room upgrades, or other contracted benefits.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">CAUTION</span> A blank concession field does not necessarily mean that no concession exists. CS generally does not manage group concessions. If a traveler or advisor reports a missing contracted benefit, gather the details and escalate through the appropriate Groups/CS leadership channel.</div>","text":"Contract The Contract area may display contractual information and timelines. Training indicated that CS should not rely solely on this section when making penalty or in-travel policy decisions, as information may not always reflect every subsequent group change. Use it for context only unless otherwise directed. Concession Information Concessions are negotiated group benefits — examples may include complimentary rooms, welcome events, room upgrades, or other contracted benefits. CAUTION A blank concession field does not necessarily mean that no concession exists. CS generally does not manage group concessions. If a traveler or advisor reports a missing contracted benefit, gather the details and escalate through the appropriate Groups/CS leadership channel."},{"id":"19-16","heading":"19.16 CS Scope in Groups Manager","html":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>CS Uses Groups Manager To</strong></th>\n<th><strong>CS Does Not Own</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Locate groups and individual bookings</td>\n<td>Creating or contracting the group</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Research traveler and room information</td>\n<td>Managing contracted inventory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review booking components</td>\n<td>Overall group administration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review warnings/advisories</td>\n<td>Group accounting/allocation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review group and room history</td>\n<td>Pre-travel group servicing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Add manual notes</td>\n<td>Managing concessions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review contracted pricing</td>\n<td>Determining contractual penalties from Groups Manager alone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calculate approved adjustments</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Take approved payments</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review payment activity</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process approved refunds</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generate rooming lists</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review previously sent documents</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Resend documents</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The items on the right remain with the Groups Department.</p>","text":"CS Uses Groups Manager To CS Does Not Own Locate groups and individual bookings Creating or contracting the group Research traveler and room information Managing contracted inventory Review booking components Overall group administration Review warnings/advisories Group accounting/allocation Review group and room history Pre-travel group servicing Add manual notes Managing concessions Review contracted pricing Determining contractual penalties from Groups Manager alone Calculate approved adjustments Take approved payments Review payment activity Process approved refunds Generate rooming lists Review previously sent documents Resend documents The items on the right remain with the Groups Department."},{"id":"19-17","heading":"19.17 Groups Manager Quick Workflow & Reference","html":"<p>When handling a group issue:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><strong>Locate the Group</strong> — search by Group ID, or by traveler first and last name.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Open the Group</strong> — confirm the correct group, advisor, Group Coordinator, hotel, travel dates, and status.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Review Warnings/Advisories</strong> — click any applicable teal warning title.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Open Bookings</strong> — locate the specific traveler/room; if the room is not visible, select Refresh.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Open the Individual Booking</strong> — confirm travelers, room category, occupancy, bedding request, dates, and financial information.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Review History</strong> — use Group History for overall activity and notes, Booking History for room-specific research.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Troubleshoot the Issue</strong> — use the appropriate Group, Booking, Pricing, Payment, or Reports functionality.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Complete Any Approved Transaction</strong> — Bookings → PAY for booking-specific payment; Payment for payment review/refunds; Pricing for contracted rate calculations.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Document the Outcome</strong> — add the final note in Group History and identify the applicable booking number.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Quick Reference</strong></p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Need</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Where to Go</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Find group by number</td><td>Home → View Group</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Find group by traveler</td><td>Home → Search By Pax Name</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review group overview</td><td>Group</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review WARN/advisory</td><td>Group → Click teal advisory title</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Find a room/traveler</td><td>Bookings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Load missing bookings</td><td>Bookings → Refresh</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review specific booking</td><td>Bookings → Open room</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Return to overall group</td><td>Group</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review overall modification history</td><td>History</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Add CS notes</td><td>Group History</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review room-specific history</td><td>Booking → History</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review contracted pricing</td><td>Pricing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Take group-level payment</td><td>Payment → Process Credit Card</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Take room-specific payment</td><td>Bookings → PAY</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review payments by room</td><td>Payment → Show Payments for booking #</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Issue refund</td><td>Payment → Right-click card → Credit This Card</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Get rooming list</td><td>Reports → Passenger Rooming List</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Review prior documents</td><td>Reports → View Docs</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Resend documents</td><td>Reports → Generate Docs</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Key Reminders</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Agent Email is the advisor's communication email. Agent Login ID is for the group website.</p></li>\n<li><p>A crossed-out booking is generally canceled.</p></li>\n<li><p>DBL / TPL / QUAD indicate occupancy, not bedding.</p></li>\n<li><p>Bedding is request only, not guaranteed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use Sell, not Cost, when communicating pricing.</p></li>\n<li><p>Use Group History for manual CS notes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Group-level and booking-specific payments follow different paths.</p></li>\n<li><p>Filter Payment by booking number before determining refund availability.</p></li>\n<li><p>Verify the card and refund amount carefully before submitting.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select the correct hotel when generating the Passenger Rooming List.</p></li>\n<li><p>Select the correct booking before generating or resending documents.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"When handling a group issue: Locate the Group — search by Group ID, or by traveler first and last name. Open the Group — confirm the correct group, advisor, Group Coordinator, hotel, travel dates, and status. Review Warnings/Advisories — click any applicable teal warning title. Open Bookings — locate the specific traveler/room; if the room is not visible, select Refresh. Open the Individual Booking — confirm travelers, room category, occupancy, bedding request, dates, and financial information. Review History — use Group History for overall activity and notes, Booking History for room-specific research. Troubleshoot the Issue — use the appropriate Group, Booking, Pricing, Payment, or Reports functionality. Complete Any Approved Transaction — Bookings → PAY for booking-specific payment; Payment for payment review/refunds; Pricing for contracted rate calculations. Document the Outcome — add the final note in Group History and identify the applicable booking number. Quick Reference Need Where to Go Find group by number Home → View Group Find group by traveler Home → Search By Pax Name Review group overview Group Review WARN/advisory Group → Click teal advisory title Find a room/traveler Bookings Load missing bookings Bookings → Refresh Review specific booking Bookings → Open room Return to overall group Group Review overall modification history History Add CS notes Group History Review room-specific history Booking → History Review contracted pricing Pricing Take group-level payment Payment → Process Credit Card Take room-specific payment Bookings → PAY Review payments by room Payment → Show Payments for booking # Issue refund Payment → Right-click card → Credit This Card Get rooming list Reports → Passenger Rooming List Review prior documents Reports → View Docs Resend documents Reports → Generate Docs Key Reminders Agent Email is the advisor's communication email. Agent Login ID is for the group website. A crossed-out booking is generally canceled. DBL / TPL / QUAD indicate occupancy, not bedding. Bedding is request only, not guaranteed. Use Sell, not Cost, when communicating pricing. Use Group History for manual CS notes. Group-level and booking-specific payments follow different paths. Filter Payment by booking number before determining refund availability. Verify the card and refund amount carefully before submitting. Select the correct hotel when generating the Passenger Rooming List. Select the correct booking before generating or resending documents."},{"id":"19-18","heading":"19.18 Group Financial Adjustments","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Group financial adjustments should be tied to the correct individual booking and supported by the approved supplier, TSP, or Classic resolution. Do not apply a FIT Plex adjustment process to a Group booking without using the appropriate Groups Manager workflow.</div>\n<p><strong>Before you start</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Confirm the correct Group ID and Booking ID.</p></li>\n<li><p>Review the individual booking's current sell, cost, commission, payments, and history.</p></li>\n<li><p>Confirm the approved amount and whether the adjustment is supplier-funded, TSP-funded, or Classic-funded.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Adjustment controls</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Use the applicable Group financial adjustment function for the individual booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Enter the correct service/effective date associated with the adjustment.</p></li>\n<li><p>For a decrease, confirm the adjusted sell, cost, and commission reflect the approved outcome.</p></li>\n<li><p>For an increase, confirm the additional amount due and collect payment using the booking-specific payment path when appropriate.</p></li>\n<li><p>Save the adjustment and re-review the individual booking financials before processing any refund.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> The Group booking reflects the correct sell, cost, commission, payment/refund position, and the adjustment is documented in Group History.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Group financial adjustments should be tied to the correct individual booking and supported by the approved supplier, TSP, or Classic resolution. Do not apply a FIT Plex adjustment process to a Group booking without using the appropriate Groups Manager workflow. Before you start Confirm the correct Group ID and Booking ID. Review the individual booking's current sell, cost, commission, payments, and history. Confirm the approved amount and whether the adjustment is supplier-funded, TSP-funded, or Classic-funded. Adjustment controls Use the applicable Group financial adjustment function for the individual booking. Enter the correct service/effective date associated with the adjustment. For a decrease, confirm the adjusted sell, cost, and commission reflect the approved outcome. For an increase, confirm the additional amount due and collect payment using the booking-specific payment path when appropriate. Save the adjustment and re-review the individual booking financials before processing any refund. COMPLETE WHEN The Group booking reflects the correct sell, cost, commission, payment/refund position, and the adjustment is documented in Group History."},{"id":"19-19","heading":"19.19 Group Commission","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Group commission does not necessarily follow the same timing as FIT commission. Group commission is generally settled after the group has completed travel and group accounts are finalized.</div>\n<p>When a Group refund or financial adjustment occurs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Review the commission associated with the individual booking.</p></li>\n<li><p>Adjust commission when the underlying booking value changes.</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not automatically treat the change as a commission recall. Determine whether commission has actually been paid.</p></li>\n<li><p>If commission status is unclear, confirm with Groups before completing the financial treatment.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">WHY THIS MATTERS</span> A Group booking can require a commission adjustment even when there is no previously paid commission to recall.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Group commission does not necessarily follow the same timing as FIT commission. Group commission is generally settled after the group has completed travel and group accounts are finalized. When a Group refund or financial adjustment occurs: Review the commission associated with the individual booking. Adjust commission when the underlying booking value changes. Do not automatically treat the change as a commission recall. Determine whether commission has actually been paid. If commission status is unclear, confirm with Groups before completing the financial treatment. WHY THIS MATTERS A Group booking can require a commission adjustment even when there is no previously paid commission to recall."},{"id":"19-20","heading":"19.20 Group Agency Fee","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">GROUP EXCEPTION</span> CS does not add an Agency/Planning Fee to a Group booking during in-travel servicing, even when CS is taking payment for a Group modification.</div>\n<p>Group agency-fee arrangements are handled through the applicable Groups process. Do not apply the FIT in-travel Agency Fee rule to a Group booking.</p>","text":"GROUP EXCEPTION CS does not add an Agency/Planning Fee to a Group booking during in-travel servicing, even when CS is taking payment for a Group modification. Group agency-fee arrangements are handled through the applicable Groups process. Do not apply the FIT in-travel Agency Fee rule to a Group booking."}]}]},{"id":"escalation-handoff","label":"Escalation, Supplier Contact & Handoff","items":[{"id":"20","number":"20","title":"Supplier Contact & Product Escalation","fullTitle":"20. Supplier Contact & Product Escalation","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> CS investigates and works the supplier first. Product Development escalation is for Preferred suppliers only and should be used after the defined threshold, not as the first supplier contact.</div>","introText":"RULE CS investigates and works the supplier first. Product Development escalation is for Preferred suppliers only and should be used after the defined threshold, not as the first supplier contact.","blocks":[{"id":"20-1","heading":"20.1 Preferred Supplier Escalation","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Escalate a Preferred supplier issue to Product Development when the vendor is unresponsive within 72 hours of receiving the complaint or the vendor’s proposed solution does not align with Classic Vacations standards.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Preferred hotel/vendor complaint requiring leverage beyond normal CS supplier contact.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm product is Preferred.</p></li>\n<li><p>Document when complaint was sent and supplier contacts/response.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Work supplier directly and seek resolution.</p></li>\n<li><p>If no response within 72 hours, compile concise escalation.</p></li>\n<li><p>If supplier responds but solution is below CV standard, explain why and what CS recommends.</p></li>\n<li><p>Send to the current PD escalation path with booking number, facts, contact history, traveler impact, and requested outcome.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>TBO/EPS/Affiliate</td>\n<td>Expedia (EPS): dedicated phone line 800-509-7498; general inquiries A2A@chat.expediapartnersolutions.com.<br/>TBO/TPS: ops.northamerica@tbo.com.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immediate in-travel emergency</td>\n<td>Do not wait 72 hours to protect the traveler; involve CS leadership immediately while continuing supplier work.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Supplier contacts, timestamps, response, requested remedy, traveler status.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> Threshold is met or immediate traveler harm requires leadership intervention.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> PD/source owner has accepted the escalation and CS maintains traveler communication until ownership is explicit.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Escalate a Preferred supplier issue to Product Development when the vendor is unresponsive within 72 hours of receiving the complaint or the vendor’s proposed solution does not align with Classic Vacations standards. Use when: Preferred hotel/vendor complaint requiring leverage beyond normal CS supplier contact. Before you start Confirm product is Preferred. Document when complaint was sent and supplier contacts/response. Steps Work supplier directly and seek resolution. If no response within 72 hours, compile concise escalation. If supplier responds but solution is below CV standard, explain why and what CS recommends. Send to the current PD escalation path with booking number, facts, contact history, traveler impact, and requested outcome. If / Then If Then TBO/EPS/Affiliate Expedia (EPS): dedicated phone line 800-509-7498; general inquiries A2A@chat.expediapartnersolutions.com. TBO/TPS: ops.northamerica@tbo.com. Immediate in-travel emergency Do not wait 72 hours to protect the traveler; involve CS leadership immediately while continuing supplier work. Document Supplier contacts, timestamps, response, requested remedy, traveler status. ESCALATE WHEN Threshold is met or immediate traveler harm requires leadership intervention. COMPLETE WHEN PD/source owner has accepted the escalation and CS maintains traveler communication until ownership is explicit."}]},{"id":"21","number":"21","title":"Post-Travel Ownership & Handoff","fullTitle":"21. Post-Travel Ownership & Handoff","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">OWNERSHIP RULE</span> Move an inquiry to Post-Travel when the booking is on the last day of travel or already post-travel AND the issue will take more than 24 hours to resolve. A Post Travel Concern form must be completed by the travel advisor or client.</div>","introText":"OWNERSHIP RULE Move an inquiry to Post-Travel when the booking is on the last day of travel or already post-travel AND the issue will take more than 24 hours to resolve. A Post Travel Concern form must be completed by the travel advisor or client.","blocks":[{"id":"21-1","heading":"21.1 Post-Travel Handoff","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Do not leave an unresolved last-day/post-travel complaint in ordinary in-travel ownership when the resolution will require more than 24 hours.</div><p><strong>Use when:</strong> Booking is on last day or already post travel and issue requires extended supplier investigation/compensation review.</p><p><strong>Before you start</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Confirm travel status and whether a same-day/within-24-hour resolution is realistically possible.</p></li>\n</ul><p><strong>Steps</strong></p><ol>\n<li><p>Advise TA/client that the Post Travel Concern form is required.</p></li>\n<li><p>Provide form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/219a2f5e09bf46cd811b53a5bc5ad7b1</p></li>\n<li><p>Ensure current CS/Plex notes clearly summarize work already completed, supplier contacts, and outstanding ask.</p></li>\n<li><p>Set expectations: post-travel supervisor/leadership callback is within 24 hours when escalated.</p></li>\n</ol><p><strong>If / Then</strong></p><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>If</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Then</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Issue began in travel but can still be completed within 24 hours</td>\n<td>CS may finish the active resolution rather than forcing a handoff solely because travel ended.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traveler still needs immediate same-day operational help</td>\n<td>Resolve the live need first; post-travel process is for the remaining extended investigation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><p><strong>Document</strong></p><ul>\n<li><p>Reason for handoff, prior work, form advisement, outstanding action.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-warning\"><span class=\"callout-label\">ESCALATE WHEN</span> High-risk/legal/safety allegation or caller requests leadership involvement.</div><div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">COMPLETE WHEN</span> Form is submitted/advised, current record is complete, and no live traveler need remains unaddressed.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Do not leave an unresolved last-day/post-travel complaint in ordinary in-travel ownership when the resolution will require more than 24 hours. Use when: Booking is on last day or already post travel and issue requires extended supplier investigation/compensation review. Before you start Confirm travel status and whether a same-day/within-24-hour resolution is realistically possible. Steps Advise TA/client that the Post Travel Concern form is required. Provide form: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/219a2f5e09bf46cd811b53a5bc5ad7b1 Ensure current CS/Plex notes clearly summarize work already completed, supplier contacts, and outstanding ask. Set expectations: post-travel supervisor/leadership callback is within 24 hours when escalated. If / Then If Then Issue began in travel but can still be completed within 24 hours CS may finish the active resolution rather than forcing a handoff solely because travel ended. Traveler still needs immediate same-day operational help Resolve the live need first; post-travel process is for the remaining extended investigation. Document Reason for handoff, prior work, form advisement, outstanding action. ESCALATE WHEN High-risk/legal/safety allegation or caller requests leadership involvement. COMPLETE WHEN Form is submitted/advised, current record is complete, and no live traveler need remains unaddressed."},{"id":"21-2","heading":"21.2 Assigned Post-Travel File Ownership","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">OWNERSHIP RULE</span> Once a Post-Travel file has been assigned to a specialist, that specialist owns the file through completion unless leadership intentionally reassigns it.</div>\n<p>When a new email, call, Zendesk ticket, or follow-up relates to an existing Post-Travel case:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Check Plex and Zendesk for an existing Post-Travel file.</p></li>\n<li><p>Identify the assigned specialist.</p></li>\n<li><p>Add any new relevant information to the case record.</p></li>\n<li><p>Route the follow-up to the assigned owner rather than beginning a separate parallel investigation.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>New Post-Travel files are assigned according to the current CS leadership process.</p>","text":"OWNERSHIP RULE Once a Post-Travel file has been assigned to a specialist, that specialist owns the file through completion unless leadership intentionally reassigns it. When a new email, call, Zendesk ticket, or follow-up relates to an existing Post-Travel case: Check Plex and Zendesk for an existing Post-Travel file. Identify the assigned specialist. Add any new relevant information to the case record. Route the follow-up to the assigned owner rather than beginning a separate parallel investigation. New Post-Travel files are assigned according to the current CS leadership process."},{"id":"21-3","heading":"21.3 Unused Air Segment Refunds","html":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">POLICY / RULE</span> Refund investigation for unused airline segments generally occurs after travel is complete.</div>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Document the unused segment and reason it was not used.</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not promise that the airline will refund the ticket.</p></li>\n<li><p>Once travel is complete, route the matter through the Post-Travel process for airline refund investigation.</p></li>\n<li><p>Post-Travel should pursue the airline refund first.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the airline denies reimbursement, applicable TSP benefits may be considered through the appropriate claim process. CS should not guarantee the outcome of a TSP claim.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">WHY WAIT UNTIL TRAVEL IS COMPLETE</span> Remaining ticket value and segment status can change while the traveler is still using the itinerary.</div>","text":"POLICY / RULE Refund investigation for unused airline segments generally occurs after travel is complete. Document the unused segment and reason it was not used. Do not promise that the airline will refund the ticket. Once travel is complete, route the matter through the Post-Travel process for airline refund investigation. Post-Travel should pursue the airline refund first. If the airline denies reimbursement, applicable TSP benefits may be considered through the appropriate claim process. CS should not guarantee the outcome of a TSP claim. WHY WAIT UNTIL TRAVEL IS COMPLETE Remaining ticket value and segment status can change while the traveler is still using the itinerary."}]},{"id":"22","number":"22","title":"Supervisor / Leadership Escalations","fullTitle":"22. Supervisor / Leadership Escalations","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">CALLBACK STANDARD</span> Urgent/in-travel: immediate takeover if on-duty leadership is available; otherwise callback within 1 hour. Non-urgent and Post-Travel: callback within 24 hours.</div>","introText":"CALLBACK STANDARD Urgent/in-travel: immediate takeover if on-duty leadership is available; otherwise callback within 1 hour. Non-urgent and Post-Travel: callback within 24 hours.","blocks":[{"id":"22-1","heading":"22.1 Escalate for Decision, Not for Avoidance","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Attempt normal investigation and resolution first unless immediate risk requires leadership.</p></li>\n<li><p>When escalating, include your recommended solution—not just “customer wants a manager.”</p></li>\n<li><p>Do not promise an outcome leadership has not approved.</p></li>\n<li><p>For an abusive caller who cannot be de-escalated after reasonable attempts, contact leadership and document the behavior objectively.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the normal owner is unavailable and the issue is time-sensitive, do not wait solely because the preferred contact is offline. Escalate through CS leadership, who can determine the approved alternate or after-hours path.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Attempt normal investigation and resolution first unless immediate risk requires leadership. When escalating, include your recommended solution—not just “customer wants a manager.” Do not promise an outcome leadership has not approved. For an abusive caller who cannot be de-escalated after reasonable attempts, contact leadership and document the behavior objectively. If the normal owner is unavailable and the issue is time-sensitive, do not wait solely because the preferred contact is offline. Escalate through CS leadership, who can determine the approved alternate or after-hours path."},{"id":"22-2","heading":"22.2 Minimum Escalation Package","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Booking number and traveler/advisor.</p></li>\n<li><p>Current location/travel status and urgency.</p></li>\n<li><p>One-paragraph factual summary.</p></li>\n<li><p>What CS verified and who was contacted.</p></li>\n<li><p>Supplier/internal responses.</p></li>\n<li><p>Financial exposure and authority already used.</p></li>\n<li><p>Exact ask from caller.</p></li>\n<li><p>Your recommended next step.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Booking number and traveler/advisor. Current location/travel status and urgency. One-paragraph factual summary. What CS verified and who was contacted. Supplier/internal responses. Financial exposure and authority already used. Exact ask from caller. Your recommended next step."}]}]},{"id":"documentation","label":"Documentation & Remarks","items":[{"id":"23","number":"23","title":"Documentation & Remarks","fullTitle":"23. Documentation & Remarks","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-policy\"><span class=\"callout-label\">RULE</span> Notes should be concise enough to scan and detailed enough to continue the case. Keep them objective and professional; Plex notes can be viewed by other internal teams, including Sales/BDMs.</div>","introText":"RULE Notes should be concise enough to scan and detailed enough to continue the case. Keep them objective and professional; Plex notes can be viewed by other internal teams, including Sales/BDMs.","blocks":[{"id":"23-1","heading":"23.1 Required Note Content","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Reason for contact / complaint.</p></li>\n<li><p>Current traveler impact.</p></li>\n<li><p>What booking history showed.</p></li>\n<li><p>Supplier/internal party contacted and result.</p></li>\n<li><p>What was promised or explicitly not promised.</p></li>\n<li><p>Financial impact: refund, penalty, goodwill, FTC, commission, payment/VCC.</p></li>\n<li><p>Advisor/traveler decision or approval.</p></li>\n<li><p>Next action, owner, and follow-up timing.</p></li>\n</ul>","text":"Reason for contact / complaint. Current traveler impact. What booking history showed. Supplier/internal party contacted and result. What was promised or explicitly not promised. Financial impact: refund, penalty, goodwill, FTC, commission, payment/VCC. Advisor/traveler decision or approval. Next action, owner, and follow-up timing."},{"id":"23-2","heading":"23.2 Note-Writing Standard","html":"<ul>\n<li><p>Use short, clear chronology or bullets rather than a long narrative.</p></li>\n<li><p>Separate confirmed facts from traveler allegations or assumptions.</p></li>\n<li><p>Avoid emotional/editorial language.</p></li>\n<li><p>If a prior note is ambiguous, clarify the point rather than copying it forward.</p></li>\n<li><p>When commission protection/goodwill/FTC is used, record amount already used so the next specialist knows remaining authority.</p></li>\n</ul><div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><span class=\"callout-label\">TEST YOUR NOTE</span> Could another CS specialist pick up this booking with no verbal handoff and know exactly what happened and what to do next? If not, the documentation is not complete.</div>","text":"Use short, clear chronology or bullets rather than a long narrative. Separate confirmed facts from traveler allegations or assumptions. Avoid emotional/editorial language. If a prior note is ambiguous, clarify the point rather than copying it forward. When commission protection/goodwill/FTC is used, record amount already used so the next specialist knows remaining authority. TEST YOUR NOTE Could another CS specialist pick up this booking with no verbal handoff and know exactly what happened and what to do next? If not, the documentation is not complete."},{"id":"23-3","heading":"23.3 CS Remark Code Quick Reference","html":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Situation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Remark Code</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>In-travel Customer Service contact/work</td><td>AFYK</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General informational/non-in-travel CS note that is not part of an active Post-Travel case</td><td>AFYI</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>AFYK should be used for in-travel CS work regardless of whether the interaction occurred by phone, email, chat, or SMS. Although the system description may reference a call, the operational use is broader in Customer Service.</p>\n<p>AFYI is appropriate for informational/non-in-travel documentation when the activity is not being managed as an active Post-Travel file.</p>\n<p>Continue to document the actual issue, action, financial impact, ownership, and next step in addition to selecting the correct remark code.</p>","text":"Situation Remark Code In-travel Customer Service contact/work AFYK General informational/non-in-travel CS note that is not part of an active Post-Travel case AFYI AFYK should be used for in-travel CS work regardless of whether the interaction occurred by phone, email, chat, or SMS. Although the system description may reference a call, the operational use is broader in Customer Service. AFYI is appropriate for informational/non-in-travel documentation when the activity is not being managed as an active Post-Travel file. Continue to document the actual issue, action, financial impact, ownership, and next step in addition to selecting the correct remark code."}]}]},{"id":"reference","label":"Quick Reference & Routing","items":[{"id":"24","number":"24","title":"Finance Operations Routing","fullTitle":"24. Finance Operations Routing","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">FINANCE VS. ACCOUNTING</span> Finance Operations = day-to-day vendor payment, TA commissions, refunds, chargebacks, VCC/CYBS support, vendor setup/updates. Accounting = back-end reconciliation, reporting, AR, audits, financial statements, legal compliance/control, and record keeping.</div><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Need</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Route / Action</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Refund / urgent refund / CYBS request</td>\n<td>sjctafinance@classicvacations.com. For expedited refund include booking number, last 4 of card, amount, and reason.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Urgent refund</td>\n<td>Finance guide: email sjctafinance@classicvacations.com and copy Tara Cardona and Lina Hernandez.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VCC support / payment detail</td>\n<td>Smartsheet: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Urgent CAD VCC</td>\n<td>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finance queue</td>\n<td>Monday–Friday 8:00 AM–5:00 PM; (408) 794-3200.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vendor new/past-due invoice, discrepancy, cancellation penalty</td>\n<td>cv_invoices@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vendor prepayment invoices</td>\n<td>sjcprepay@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Corporate expenses</td>\n<td>corp-payables@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chargeback question posted to booking</td>\n<td>Finance guide lists hernandezp@classicvacations.com and copy narchuleta@classicvacations.com.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>After-hours/weekend urgent VCC</td>\n<td>CS agent → CS leadership → Teams channel “VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support.”</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"FINANCE VS. ACCOUNTING Finance Operations = day-to-day vendor payment, TA commissions, refunds, chargebacks, VCC/CYBS support, vendor setup/updates. Accounting = back-end reconciliation, reporting, AR, audits, financial statements, legal compliance/control, and record keeping. Need Route / Action Refund / urgent refund / CYBS request sjctafinance@classicvacations.com. For expedited refund include booking number, last 4 of card, amount, and reason. Urgent refund Finance guide: email sjctafinance@classicvacations.com and copy Tara Cardona and Lina Hernandez. VCC support / payment detail Smartsheet: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b Urgent CAD VCC https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8 Finance queue Monday–Friday 8:00 AM–5:00 PM; (408) 794-3200. Vendor new/past-due invoice, discrepancy, cancellation penalty cv_invoices@classicvacations.com Vendor prepayment invoices sjcprepay@classicvacations.com Corporate expenses corp-payables@classicvacations.com Chargeback question posted to booking Finance guide lists hernandezp@classicvacations.com and copy narchuleta@classicvacations.com. After-hours/weekend urgent VCC CS agent → CS leadership → Teams channel “VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support.”","blocks":[]},{"id":"25","number":"25","title":"Quick Policy Library","fullTitle":"25. Quick Policy Library","introHtml":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Policy</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Rule</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Customer refund SLA</td>\n<td>7–10 business days.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commission payout timeframe</td>\n<td>7–14 business days was clarified as commission-payout timing, not customer refund timing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CS goodwill authority</td>\n<td>$100 per booking; leadership approval is required if the adjustment would reduce CV net margin below 5%, regardless of the dollar amount.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CS FTC authority</td>\n<td>$250 per booking, FIT or Groups; above requires leadership.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>In-travel commission protection</td>\n<td>Up to $100 total per booking; TSP required; in-travel changes only.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Urgent leadership callback</td>\n<td>Immediate if available; otherwise within 1 hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non-urgent/post-travel callback</td>\n<td>Within 24 hours.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PD escalation</td>\n<td>Preferred only; unresponsive within 72 hours after complaint receipt OR solution below CV standard.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Post-travel handoff</td>\n<td>Last day/post travel + &gt;24 hours to resolve; TA/client submits Post Travel Concern form.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>In-travel agency fee</td>\n<td>Requires an actual modification that requires payment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Partial in-travel hotel refund</td>\n<td>Check free-night promotions and minimum-stay conditions before calculating the average nightly rate.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TSP claim promises</td>\n<td>Do not promise insurance reimbursement; refer claim specifics to TripMate.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VCC direct charge</td>\n<td>Urgent: contact property for reversal and escalate payment support.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TBO/EPS escalation</td>\n<td>Use respective source escalation channel; not PD.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goodwill margin guardrail</td>\n<td>Agent authority is up to $100 per booking, but leadership approval is required if the adjustment would reduce CV net margin below 5%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supplier-funded refund</td>\n<td>Adjust sell, commission as applicable, and supplier cost to the vendor-approved financial outcome.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TSP/Classic-funded refund</td>\n<td>Do not reduce supplier cost when Classic still owes the vendor.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supplier protects commission</td>\n<td>Preserve the approved commission and document supplier approval.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Client refund vs. commission</td>\n<td>Do not reduce an approved client refund solely to preserve TA commission.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Group Agency Fee</td>\n<td>CS does not add Agency/Planning Fees to Group bookings.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Group commission</td>\n<td>Verify whether commission has actually paid before treating a Group adjustment as a recall.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AFYK</td>\n<td>Use for in-travel CS interactions/work.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AFYI</td>\n<td>Use for general informational/non-in-travel CS documentation outside an active PT file.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Post-Travel ownership</td>\n<td>Assigned specialist retains ownership until completion or leadership reassignment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unused airfare</td>\n<td>Investigate unused-segment airline refunds after travel through Post-Travel.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"Policy Rule Customer refund SLA 7–10 business days. Commission payout timeframe 7–14 business days was clarified as commission-payout timing, not customer refund timing. CS goodwill authority $100 per booking; leadership approval is required if the adjustment would reduce CV net margin below 5%, regardless of the dollar amount. CS FTC authority $250 per booking, FIT or Groups; above requires leadership. In-travel commission protection Up to $100 total per booking; TSP required; in-travel changes only. Urgent leadership callback Immediate if available; otherwise within 1 hour. Non-urgent/post-travel callback Within 24 hours. PD escalation Preferred only; unresponsive within 72 hours after complaint receipt OR solution below CV standard. Post-travel handoff Last day/post travel + >24 hours to resolve; TA/client submits Post Travel Concern form. In-travel agency fee Requires an actual modification that requires payment. Partial in-travel hotel refund Check free-night promotions and minimum-stay conditions before calculating the average nightly rate. TSP claim promises Do not promise insurance reimbursement; refer claim specifics to TripMate. VCC direct charge Urgent: contact property for reversal and escalate payment support. TBO/EPS escalation Use respective source escalation channel; not PD. Goodwill margin guardrail Agent authority is up to $100 per booking, but leadership approval is required if the adjustment would reduce CV net margin below 5%. Supplier-funded refund Adjust sell, commission as applicable, and supplier cost to the vendor-approved financial outcome. TSP/Classic-funded refund Do not reduce supplier cost when Classic still owes the vendor. Supplier protects commission Preserve the approved commission and document supplier approval. Client refund vs. commission Do not reduce an approved client refund solely to preserve TA commission. Group Agency Fee CS does not add Agency/Planning Fees to Group bookings. Group commission Verify whether commission has actually paid before treating a Group adjustment as a recall. AFYK Use for in-travel CS interactions/work. AFYI Use for general informational/non-in-travel CS documentation outside an active PT file. Post-Travel ownership Assigned specialist retains ownership until completion or leadership reassignment. Unused airfare Investigate unused-segment airline refunds after travel through Post-Travel.","blocks":[]},{"id":"26","number":"26","title":"Completion Standards by Work Type","fullTitle":"26. Completion Standards by Work Type","introHtml":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Work type</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Complete only when…</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Hotel relocation</td>\n<td>Replacement is confirmed/safe; original hotel disposition known; related components updated; financial action routed; traveler/advisor advised.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transfer issue</td>\n<td>Traveler has transport; future pickups corrected; refund/supplier issue resolved or owned.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Air disruption</td>\n<td>Current flight confirmed; transfer/hotel/tour/car ripple effect reviewed and updated.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Refund</td>\n<td>Booking is balanced; adjustment matches approval; refund workflow submitted; advisor advised of amount/timing/commission impact.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goodwill</td>\n<td>Amount within authority or approved; adjustment posted; prior usage checked; caller advised.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FTC</td>\n<td>Credit created within authority/approved; terms communicated; documented.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Commission protection</td>\n<td>TSP verified; qualifying in-travel change; prior usage checked; total protection does not exceed $100.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VCC issue</td>\n<td>Finance/vendor ticket submitted; active traveler risk addressed; after-hours escalation used if required.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PD escalation</td>\n<td>Preferred confirmed; threshold met; contact history and recommended outcome included; owner accepted.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Post-Travel</td>\n<td>Live need addressed; form provided/submitted; complete notes; extended case intentionally handed off.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Zendesk ticket</td>\n<td>System action done; caller has resolution/expectation; follow-up owned; correct status; Plex updated when booking-impacting.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"Work type Complete only when… Hotel relocation Replacement is confirmed/safe; original hotel disposition known; related components updated; financial action routed; traveler/advisor advised. Transfer issue Traveler has transport; future pickups corrected; refund/supplier issue resolved or owned. Air disruption Current flight confirmed; transfer/hotel/tour/car ripple effect reviewed and updated. Refund Booking is balanced; adjustment matches approval; refund workflow submitted; advisor advised of amount/timing/commission impact. Goodwill Amount within authority or approved; adjustment posted; prior usage checked; caller advised. FTC Credit created within authority/approved; terms communicated; documented. Commission protection TSP verified; qualifying in-travel change; prior usage checked; total protection does not exceed $100. VCC issue Finance/vendor ticket submitted; active traveler risk addressed; after-hours escalation used if required. PD escalation Preferred confirmed; threshold met; contact history and recommended outcome included; owner accepted. Post-Travel Live need addressed; form provided/submitted; complete notes; extended case intentionally handed off. Zendesk ticket System action done; caller has resolution/expectation; follow-up owned; correct status; Plex updated when booking-impacting.","blocks":[]},{"id":"27","number":"27","title":"Working Glossary","fullTitle":"27. Working Glossary","introHtml":"<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Term</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Meaning</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>CS</td>\n<td>Customer Service.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plex</td>\n<td>Primary reservation platform used for booking servicing/history.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TSP</td>\n<td>Travel Smart Plan / trip protection product on the booking.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TripMate</td>\n<td>Insurance/claims administrator referenced in training for the insurance portion of TSP.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VCC</td>\n<td>Virtual credit card used to pay/secure applicable supplier bookings. Training sometimes used “BCC”; this guide standardizes on VCC.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CAD</td>\n<td>Manual/competitive booking process used when a component is built/secured outside normal live inventory.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>FTC</td>\n<td>Future Travel Credit used as service recovery.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Line-Item Adjustment</td>\n<td>Financial change tied to a specific component.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Booking-Level Adjustment</td>\n<td>Whole-booking commission or CS/TA goodwill/error-related financial handling.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preferred</td>\n<td>Classic Preferred supplier/product eligible for PD escalation under Section 20.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>EPS</td>\n<td>Affiliate/Expedia source referenced in training.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Groups Manager</td>\n<td>System/resource used to review Group booking/rooming information.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Record Locator</td>\n<td>Airline confirmation used to view current flight record.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mod History</td>\n<td>Booking modification history used to investigate prior changes.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"Term Meaning CS Customer Service. Plex Primary reservation platform used for booking servicing/history. TSP Travel Smart Plan / trip protection product on the booking. TripMate Insurance/claims administrator referenced in training for the insurance portion of TSP. VCC Virtual credit card used to pay/secure applicable supplier bookings. Training sometimes used “BCC”; this guide standardizes on VCC. CAD Manual/competitive booking process used when a component is built/secured outside normal live inventory. FTC Future Travel Credit used as service recovery. Line-Item Adjustment Financial change tied to a specific component. Booking-Level Adjustment Whole-booking commission or CS/TA goodwill/error-related financial handling. Preferred Classic Preferred supplier/product eligible for PD escalation under Section 20. EPS Affiliate/Expedia source referenced in training. Groups Manager System/resource used to review Group booking/rooming information. Record Locator Airline confirmation used to view current flight record. Mod History Booking modification history used to investigate prior changes.","blocks":[]},{"id":"appendix-a-current-routing-directory","number":null,"title":"Appendix A. Current Routing Directory","fullTitle":"Appendix A. Current Routing Directory","introHtml":"<div class=\"callout callout-info\"><span class=\"callout-label\">MAINTENANCE</span> This is the most time-sensitive section. Revalidate whenever teams, aliases, phone numbers, Smartsheets, or ownership change.</div><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\"/>\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Topic</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Current route</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>CS main mailbox</td>\n<td>sjccustomerservice@classicvacations.com (from current CS leadership email signature).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finance Operations</td>\n<td>sjctafinance@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finance queue</td>\n<td>(408) 794-3200, Monday–Friday 8:00 AM–5:00 PM</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VCC vendor request</td>\n<td>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Urgent CAD VCC</td>\n<td>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Weekend urgent VCC</td>\n<td>CS leadership → Teams: VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Post Travel Concern</td>\n<td>https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/219a2f5e09bf46cd811b53a5bc5ad7b1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vendor invoices</td>\n<td>cv_invoices@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vendor prepay</td>\n<td>sjcprepay@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Corporate payables</td>\n<td>corp-payables@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chargebacks</td>\n<td>hernandezp@classicvacations.com; copy narchuleta@classicvacations.com</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preferred supplier escalation</td>\n<td>Current Product Development escalation channel after Section 20 threshold.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TBO / EPS</td>\n<td>Use current dedicated TBO/EPS escalation channels.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","introText":"MAINTENANCE This is the most time-sensitive section. Revalidate whenever teams, aliases, phone numbers, Smartsheets, or ownership change. Topic Current route CS main mailbox sjccustomerservice@classicvacations.com (from current CS leadership email signature). Finance Operations sjctafinance@classicvacations.com Finance queue (408) 794-3200, Monday–Friday 8:00 AM–5:00 PM VCC vendor request https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/5e7a13c6d51f47329169689a3515335b Urgent CAD VCC https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/0e43972dc1ad4261951536f8dc699eb8 Weekend urgent VCC CS leadership → Teams: VCC Urgent Requests-Weekend Support Post Travel Concern https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/219a2f5e09bf46cd811b53a5bc5ad7b1 Vendor invoices cv_invoices@classicvacations.com Vendor prepay sjcprepay@classicvacations.com Corporate payables corp-payables@classicvacations.com Chargebacks hernandezp@classicvacations.com; copy narchuleta@classicvacations.com Preferred supplier escalation Current Product Development escalation channel after Section 20 threshold. TBO / EPS Use current dedicated TBO/EPS escalation channels.","blocks":[]}]}];
